offeredAs; a shell read of a command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place sed, a redirect and a heredoc line do not; a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes correctly; the Codex reader opens the resolved file; the holdout guard reads the live capture; docs agree with code. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Closing round of code review pass four of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-4c.txt lists the files of the fix commit, one per line as area TAB path, for the commit range 48f03b5013..868b185e76. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: scorer-attach-close-4c reviews the lines whose area is scorer-attach, accuracy-runner-close-4c the lines whose area is accuracy-runner, plus the shared docs that describe them. This round confirms the fixes for SAC4B-P1-001, SAC4B-P2-001, AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002 (adjudicated in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt) and for the findings in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md and looks for defects the fixes added. Read that report first and do not re-report a finding it rejects or records as accepted unless you show a new input that breaks it. Read the diff with git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 48f03b5013 868b185e76 -- <path>. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. Check: a refusal over an or-list, with or without the article and the word command, and a question over an or-list carry no command while a request over a list keeps its command; both run-log writers keep offeredAs; a shell read of a command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place sed, a redirect and a heredoc line do not; a heredoc end word with a hyphen or a dot closes correctly; the Codex reader opens the resolved file; the holdout guard reads the live capture; docs agree with code. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4c.txt 2>&1\", \"workdir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794682806182,"end":1794682806564}}}}
