{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683042241,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db71b4b4001wZoOEimiCGEs6r","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db71a98a001FDyNux153OBlg9","type":"tool","id":"call_1f3f5a4066cc404ab12033f1","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-close-4c lineage\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking the closing round of review pass four for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\nversion: 1.11.14.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-close-4c lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\niteration before any review action.\n\n### Ownership\n\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nClosing round of review pass four of\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` in the\n`scorer-attach` area, over the fix commit range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\n\nScope: the `scorer-attach` rows of `review/review-scope-4c.txt` — `command-attach.ts` and\n`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` — and the shared docs that describe them. The\n`accuracy-runner` row (the routing-accuracy `README.md`) belongs to the sibling lineage and is\nread here only as doc context. The round confirms the fixes for SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4B-P2-001\nand for the verified findings in `review/verify-4/report.md`, and looks for defects the fixes\nadded. A finding that report rejects, or records as an accepted limit, is not re-raised without\na new input that breaks it.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — new or-list grammar in `commandOnlyMentioned`, refusal/question/request split\n- [ ] D2 Security — untrusted prompt reading, regex backtracking, path/name boundaries\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — docs and stored expectations vs the code's claimed behaviour\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — comment accuracy, test pinning, duplicated grammar\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The accuracy-runner harness, its run-log writers and session readers are the sibling\n  lineage's code scope; this lineage checks only that its own scorer surface agrees with them.\n- Hook, plugin, render and doctor-command code is outside both scope rows.\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 3; the terminal record must carry `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [none yet] | [pending] | [0] | [not started] |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:saturated-directions -->\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:saturated-directions -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Investigated and eliminated angles are consolidated here from iteration dead-end data]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the new `COMMAND_OR_LIST` grammar in `commandOnlyMentioned` and the leads it now joins (`command-attach.ts:376-440`), plus the added or-list rows in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-215`.\n- Reason: the closing round's only scorer-attach code change is that grammar; SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4B-P2-001 must be reproduced, and any defect the change added must be found before synthesis.\n- Rotation status: not started.\n- Required evidence: a probe run of the real module over refusal, question and request rows, including the article and `command` forms and multi-word `/doctor:` commands.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (module under review), `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (its unit tests).\n- Behavior claims: a refusal or a question over an or-list carries no command; a request over an or-list keeps its command; the article `the` and the word `command` may appear on a listed item; the command after the last `or` may carry `the`.\n- Findings to confirm: SAC4B-P1-001 (a refusal over `A or the B command` kept B), SAC4B-P2-001 (a question over an or-list kept its second command).\n- Prior report: `review/verify-4/report.md` — 3 P1 and 15 P2 confirmed, 3 rejected. Rejected and accepted-limit findings are not re-raised without a new input.\n- Commands that attach a command live in `MODE_COMMANDS` (`sk-design`, `sk-doc`, `system-deep-loop`); multi-word commands exist only under `/doctor:` and are typed-command rows.\n- Conventions: comment explains the grammar it guards; every new rule carries a test row.\n- Out-of-scope areas: the run-log writers (`command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`) and the accuracy runner belong to the sibling lineage.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | 0 | [not checked yet] |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | 0 | [not checked yet] |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no agent surface in this lineage's scope |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no runtime mirror in this lineage's scope |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | 0 | [feature-catalog docs to check] |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no playbook surface in this lineage's scope |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | [pending] | [0] | [0/0/0] | [not started] |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | [pending] | [0] | [0/0/0] | [not started] |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 3\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-attach-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-14T20:05:00Z\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-close-4c lineage\\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking the closing round of review pass four for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\\nversion: 1.11.14.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-close-4c lineage\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\\niteration before any review action.\\n\\n### Ownership\\n\\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nClosing round of review pass four of\\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` in the\\n`scorer-attach` area, over the fix commit range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\\n\\nScope: the `scorer-attach` rows of `review/review-scope-4c.txt` — `command-attach.ts` and\\n`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` — and the shared docs that describe them. The\\n`accuracy-runner` row (the routing-accuracy `README.md`) belongs to the sibling lineage and is\\nread here only as doc context. The round confirms the fixes for SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4B-P2-001\\nand for the verified findings in `review/verify-4/report.md`, and looks for defects the fixes\\nadded. A finding that report rejects, or records as an accepted limit, is not re-raised without\\na new input that breaks it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — new or-list grammar in `commandOnlyMentioned`, refusal/question/request split\\n- [ ] D2 Security — untrusted prompt reading, regex backtracking, path/name boundaries\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — docs and stored expectations vs the code's claimed behaviour\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — comment accuracy, test pinning, duplicated grammar\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- The accuracy-runner harness, its run-log writers and session readers are the sibling\\n  lineage's code scope; this lineage checks only that its own scorer surface agrees with them.\\n- Hook, plugin, render and doctor-command code is outside both scope rows.\\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold.\\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 3; the terminal record must carry `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| [none yet] | [pending] | [0] | [not started] |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:saturated-directions -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:saturated-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Investigated and eliminated angles are consolidated here from iteration dead-end data]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: the new `COMMAND_OR_LIST` grammar in `commandOnlyMentioned` and the leads it now joins (`command-attach.ts:376-440`), plus the added or-list rows in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-215`.\\n- Reason: the closing round's only scorer-attach code change is that grammar; SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4B-P2-001 must be reproduced, and any defect the change added must be found before synthesis.\\n- Rotation status: not started.\\n- Required evidence: a probe run of the real module over refusal, question and request rows, including the article and `command` forms and multi-word `/doctor:` commands.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (module under review), `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (its unit tests).\\n- Behavior claims: a refusal or a question over an or-list carries no command; a request over an or-list keeps its command; the article `the` and the word `command` may appear on a listed item; the command after the last `or` may carry `the`.\\n- Findings to confirm: SAC4B-P1-001 (a refusal over `A or the B command` kept B), SAC4B-P2-001 (a question over an or-list kept its second command).\\n- Prior report: `review/verify-4/report.md` — 3 P1 and 15 P2 confirmed, 3 rejected. Rejected and accepted-limit findings are not re-raised without a new input.\\n- Commands that attach a command live in `MODE_COMMANDS` (`sk-design`, `sk-doc`, `system-deep-loop`); multi-word commands exist only under `/doctor:` and are typed-command rows.\\n- Conventions: comment explains the grammar it guards; every new rule carries a test row.\\n- Out-of-scope areas: the run-log writers (`command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`) and the accuracy runner belong to the sibling lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | 0 | [not checked yet] |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | 0 | [not checked yet] |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no agent surface in this lineage's scope |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no runtime mirror in this lineage's scope |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | 0 | [feature-catalog docs to check] |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no playbook surface in this lineage's scope |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | [pending] | [0] | [0/0/0] | [not started] |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | [pending] | [0] | [0/0/0] | [not started] |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 3\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-attach-close-4c-1794682797954-pcdanq, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: spec-folder\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-14T20:05:00Z\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683024564,"end":1794683042241}}}}
