{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683207919,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db747c79001DXHwOQ28ult7q0","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db73f37b0014ZgL5nxBnFQY8S","type":"tool","id":"call_1a9dced744a949b48f4eb2dc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"T028\\|T029\\|T030\" -A 8 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md 2>/dev/null | head -60; echo \"===SPEC===\"; grep -rn \"T028\\|T029\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md | head","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"81:- [x] T028 Carry the article form through the or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its comment). Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P1-001: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still printed `[[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"],...]`. This task changes that one constant and its comment and nothing else in `CA`. The new value is `'(?:(?:the )?\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?: command)?,? or (?:the )?)*'`, so a listed command may carry `the` before it and `command` after it, and the command after the last `or` may carry `the`. Test first: in `CAT`, add four rows to the table of the case `reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list`: `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` and `['never use the /create:readme command or the /create:feature-catalog command', '/create:feature-catalog']`, and one row to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`: `['use /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four refusal rows fail, then change the constant and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 5 more tests than before, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 4 failed of 138, then 138 of 138. Constant matches the task value, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, no wrongly refused command in an edge probe\n82:- [x] T029 Read a question over an or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` function `commandOnlyMentioned` and the comment of `COMMAND_OR_LIST`). After T028. Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P2-001: `should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?` and `is /create:agent or /create:readme better?` each printed `/create:readme` with policy `start`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, insert `${COMMAND_OR_LIST}` directly before `${name}` in the `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` test and in both `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` tests, three insertions and nothing else in the function, and change the first sentence of the comment above `COMMAND_OR_LIST` so it says a refusal or a question over an or-list covers every command the list joins. Test first: in `CAT`, add a table case `reads %s as a question about %s through an or-list` with the rows `['should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?', '/create:readme']`, `['is /create:agent or /create:readme better?', '/create:readme']` and `['what does /create:agent or /create:readme do?', '/create:readme']`, each expecting `commandOnlyMentioned` to return `true`, and add the row `['the next step is /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme']` to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`. Run the file and see the three question rows fail, then make the change and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 3 failed of 142, then 142 of 142. Three insertions of COMMAND_OR_LIST, comment reworded, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, a later unled request and a mid-sentence is still read as requests\n83-\n84-### Lane O: the two run-log writers\n85-\n86-- [x] T006 [P] Keep `offeredAs` on a backfilled line (`COT`, then `CO` function `backfillRunLog`). After T003. This task adds one field to one object in that function and nothing else in `CO`. Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head')`, built as the case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once` builds its two lines, whose `replay` returns `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null }` when `sessionId` is `backfill-row-one` and `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }` otherwise, and which expects the first written line's `offeredAs` to be `'partner'` and the second's to be `null`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see `offeredAs` read `undefined`. Then in the `else` branch that builds `nextLine`, directly after `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,`, add `offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: where the command sat in the head travels with it, because a command on the partner side was shown and not offered. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `recomputes only the brief when the offers are already recorded` still passes, `node --check $CO` exits 0 and `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 30 (expected undefined to be partner), then 30 of 30. BACKFILL prints HAS offeredAs, node --check 0, typecheck 0\n87-- [x] T007 Keep `offeredAs` on a live run line (`CBG`, then `R` new exported function `offerLineFields` and its one call in `runTurn`). After T006. `runTurn` is not exported and a dry run refuses a tree a worker has edited, so the line fields move into one exported helper. Test first: in `CBG`, add `offerLineFields` to the import from `../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and add `describe('offerLineFields')` with `it('copies the offered command, its policy and where it sat')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' }`, and `it('writes null where the replay found no offer')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null }`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see both fail because the function is not exported. Then export `offerLineFields(offer)` from `R`, which returns `{ offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null, offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null, offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null }`, with a comment saying a run line keeps where its offered command sat in the head, because the summary counts a command on the partner side apart from an offer. In `runTurn`, replace the two lines `offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand,` and `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,` inside the `appendRunLine` call with `...offerLineFields(offer),`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F '...offerLineFields(offer),' $R` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,' $R` prints nothing and `node --check $R` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 15 (offerLineFields is not a function), then 15 of 15. node --check 0, typecheck 0\n88-\n89-### Lane S: the transcript scorer\n90-\n--\n106:- [x] T030 Count the four fields in every sentence and name the line that carries none (`RA`). After T013. Added by T025 after the confirming round found AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002. In the sentence that starts `` `run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields``, replace `three fields` with `four fields`. In the runner's row, replace ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` `` with ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered` ``. Directly after the line `Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:` and its list, at the end of the `briefDelivered` item, add the sentence `A line written when the head moved stops before the offer is read, so it carries none of the four and holds headMoved instead.` Verify: `rg -c 'three fields' $RAD/README.md` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'carries none of the four' $RAD/README.md` prints 1 and `rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`' $RAD/README.md` prints 1. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three edits, rg three fields prints nothing, the other two rg checks print 1, the head-moved sentence matches the code\n107-\n108-### Lane E: four documents\n109-\n110-- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prin