 in `CBG`, add `offerLineFields` to the import from `../scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and add `describe('offerLineFields')` with `it('copies the offered command, its policy and where it sat')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' }`, and `it('writes null where the replay found no offer')`, expecting `offerLineFields({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' })` to equal `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null }`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see both fail because the function is not exported. Then export `offerLineFields(offer)` from `R`, which returns `{ offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null, offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null, offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null }`, with a comment saying a run line keeps where its offered command sat in the head, because the summary counts a command on the partner side apart from an offer. In `runTurn`, replace the two lines `offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand,` and `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,` inside the `appendRunLine` call with `...offerLineFields(offer),`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F '...offerLineFields(offer),' $R` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy,' $R` prints nothing and `node --check $R` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 2 failed of 15 (offerLineFields is not a function), then 15 of 15. node --check 0, typecheck 0\n88-\n89-### Lane S: the transcript scorer\n90-\n--\n106:- [x] T030 Count the four fields in every sentence and name the line that carries none (`RA`). After T013. Added by T025 after the confirming round found AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002. In the sentence that starts `` `run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields``, replace `three fields` with `four fields`. In the runner's row, replace ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` `` with ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered` ``. Directly after the line `Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:` and its list, at the end of the `briefDelivered` item, add the sentence `A line written when the head moved stops before the offer is read, so it carries none of the four and holds headMoved instead.` Verify: `rg -c 'three fields' $RAD/README.md` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'carries none of the four' $RAD/README.md` prints 1 and `rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`' $RAD/README.md` prints 1. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three edits, rg three fields prints nothing, the other two rg checks print 1, the head-moved sentence matches the code\n107-\n108-### Lane E: four documents\n109-\n110-- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'A hub below the head leaves' $FA` prints 1, and `rg -n -F 'index === 0' $ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` prints one line. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact two-sentence replacement, both rg counts 1, index === 0 at advisor-recommend.ts:478\n111-- [x] T015 Correct the case count of the meaning anchor test (`FM`). After T014. In the row for `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, replace `17 cases:` with `28 cases:`. Before the edit, run `rg -c -e '^\\s*it\\(' $ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. When it prints another number than 28, write that number in place of 28 and say so in the evidence. Verify: `rg -c -F '28 cases:' $FM` prints 1, or the printed count does, and `rg -c -F '17 cases' $FM` prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: it( count 28, vitest 28 of 28, 28 cases: prints 1, 17 cases prints nothing\n112-- [x] T016 Name the child form on the companion line (`AR`). After T015. In the paragraph that holds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)`, replace `where the policy is run, start or ask` with ``where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'parent-named only' $AR` prints 1, `rg -c -F \"PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only'\" $ADV/lib/render.ts` prints 1 and the em dash and semicolon count of `AR` equals its count at `BASE`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: parent-named only prints 1, matches policyWord and companionCommandLabel in render.ts\n113-- [x] T017 Name the by-hand fix for a malformed router row (`DP`). After T016. Directly below the row that starts ``| `A11` reports missing router rows``, add the row: ``| `A11` reports a malformed router row | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds missing rows only and never rewrites one, so fix the row in `REPO RULES.md` by hand until its cell count matches the header, then run the check again |``. Verify: `rg -c -F 'reports a malformed router row' $DP` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'malformed' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` prints at least 1 and `DT` reports `fail 0`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact row below the A11 missing-rows row. DT printed 1220 passed 1 failed on the stale advisor dist (doctor-phrase-reach), outside this file; T018 reruns DT after the build\n114-<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n===SPEC===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"T028\\\\|T029\\\\|T030\\\" -A 8 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md 2>/dev/null | head -60; echo \\\"===SPEC===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"T028\\\\|T029\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md | head\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683206777,"end":1794683207919}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683208857,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db74795f001562al5fSDkrYhQ","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db73f37b0014ZgL5nxBnFQY8S","type":"tool","id":"call_2c06cfa725eb40518fc9d6b8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"or-list\\|or list\" --include=*.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md:16:The CLI front door `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` is the only surface over the advisor daemon contract. The CLI exposes 9 commands through a hand-maintained manifest whose schemas are held byte-identical to the server `TOOL_DEFINITIONS` by a dedicated parity suite (`tests/skill-advisor-cli-manifest-parity.vitest.ts`) — drift between the two registries fails tests rather than shipping. `skill-advisor list-tools --format json` returns `{ status: \"ok\", data: { count: 9 } }` as the runtime parity check. The Python facade `skill_advisor.py` stayed untouched, and the OpenCode plugin plus the Claude/OpenCode prompt-submit hooks shell out to the CLI.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.18.1.0.md:3:description: \"A show or list question about the decision-capture queue, a chat candidate or the decision record now routes to spec-kit instead of nowhere, and a request to research or build something about decisions is left alone.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/tar/README.md:343:to extract or list, so they're equivalent to a filter that tests if\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:80:- [x] T017 Count the fit rows apart from every other tally (`$CRS`, then `$CAP` function `headCarriesCommand` and the row loop of `scoreCommandCorpus`). After T005. Test first: add the case `counts the sealed fit rows and publishes none`, which asserts `live.attachedMetrics.fit.skillOnly.total` is 24, `fit.decline.total` is 24, each of the four `fit.decline.byKind` totals is 6, every `carried` is at most its `total`, and no key of `live.rows`, `attachedMetrics.attachedRows` or `attachedMetrics.typedRows` starts with `fit-`. It fails because `fit` is undefined. Then add `headCarriesCommand(landed, delivered)`, true when `landed[0]` is not null or `delivered` is defined. In the row loop of `scoreCommandCorpus`, once `delivered` is known, a row whose `row_type` is `skill-only` or `decline` adds 1 to the `total` of its `fit` tally, adds 1 to `carried` when `headCarriesCommand` is true, and continues to the next row, so it takes part in no other count, row map or list. Place that `continue` above the block that counts bridge agreement, so `metrics.agreement` does not count a fit row. A `decline` row also adds to the `byKind` entry named by its `decline_kind`. Publish `attachedMetrics.fit` as `{ skillOnly: { carried, total }, decline: { carried, total, byKind } }`. Verify: `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` reports the new case failed before the change and passes after it, the case `publishes no holdout row` passes, and only the `attachedMetrics` and corpus hash comparisons fail until T006. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run cannot destructure skillOnly (3 failed), after a dist rebuild 2 failed of 9, attachedMetrics and the corpus hash, both cleared by the T006 recapture. publishes no holdout row passes, typecheck exit 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:70:- [x] T003 [P] Count a shell read of a workflow document as a load (`S`, `CTS`). Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('workflowPath')`, add `it('counts a shell read of the owner entry document as a skill load')` expecting `workflowPath([ev(0, 'shell', { command: 'cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md' })], { command: '/create:agent', owner: 'sk-doc', wrote: false })` to be `'skill'`, `it('counts a shell read of the command document as a command load')` expecting `workflowPath([ev(0, 'shell', { command: 'sed -n 1,80p .opencode/commands/create/agent.md | head -40' }), ev(1, 'write', { path: '.opencode/agents/x.md' })], { command: '/create:agent', owner: 'sk-doc', wrote: true })` to be `'command'`, and `it.each(['echo .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md', 'ls .skilled/skills/sk-doc', 'cat notes.md > .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md'])('does not count %s as a load', ...)` expecting `'none'` for the first two and a value other than `'skill'` for the third. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the first two cases return `'none'` and `'improvised'`. Then in `S`, above `followedBeforeWrite`, add `const SHELL_READERS = Object.freeze(['cat', 'head', 'tail', 'sed', 'less', 'more', 'bat', 'nl', 'awk', 'rg', 'grep'])` and `function shellReadTargets(command)`, which splits the command on `;`, `&&`, `||`, `|` and line breaks, keeps each part whose first word, or first word after leading `NAME=value` words, is in `SHELL_READERS`, drops every word that follows a `>` or `>>` operator, strips one pair of surrounding quotes from each remaining word and returns the words that end in `.md`, `.yaml` or `.yml`. Give it a comment saying some runtimes read a document through the shell rather than a read tool, and that only a command that reads a file names one, so a path that is merely printed or listed is not a load. In `followedBeforeWrite`, let a `shell` event through the kind check and build `named` from `shellReadTargets(event.command)` for it. In `ownerLoadedBeforeWrite`, before the compiled-route check, return `true` for a `shell` event before the boundary when one of `shellReadTargets(command)` matches `documents`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run Tests 2 failed, 85 passed (87), expected none to be skill. Passing run Tests 87 passed (87). Opus check PASS, typecheck exit 0, scratch/verify report.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:81:- [x] T010 State the body rule in the reader README (`SRR`). After T009. In the paragraph or list that describes what a record holds, or directly below the table row for `codex.mjs` when no such paragraph exists, add this sentence word for word: ``A Codex custom tool call has no JSON arguments, so its record carries the call's body as `arguments.input`, a string.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'carries the call' $SRR` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '—|;' $SRR` prints the count it printed before the edit. Evidence: Opus check PASS: sentence word for word at README line 32, rg carries the call prints 1, em dash and semicolon count 0 before and after\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:283:| Review pass four verification, 2026-11-14 | 3 P1 and 15 P2 confirmed, 3 rejected | Opus verifier, report review/verify-4/report.md. P1: refusal over an or-list keeps the second command (SA4-P1-002), offeredAs dropped by both run-log writers, a shell read of a command document is not a start (raised from P2). fanout-merge counts 10 active P1 because it merges all 18 lineages of every pass |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:104:| Move T031 and T032 to the packet's operator list (ADR-001) | Approving Codex hooks writes the operator's own `~/.codex/config.toml`. Taken autonomously under the goal's rule D1, not by the operator |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:160:| T031 runs one Codex smoke row after operator approval, and T032 decodes its brief | Both `[B]`, moved to the packet's operator list by ADR-001 | Approval writes the operator's `~/.codex/config.toml` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:129:- [x] T031 [C] Dropped from this phase by ADR-001 and waiting on the operator: moved to the packet's operator list by ADR-001, because approving Codex hooks writes the operator's `~/.codex/config.toml`. Original task: Codex smoke: prepare one arena at this phase's commit, have the operator open `/hooks` in a Codex session there and approve each entry, then run one row through `R` with `--runtime codex --arm smoke`. Verify: `node $CK --root <arena>` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, and the rollout at the line's `locator.transcriptPath` contains `Advisor: `.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:130:- [x] T032 Dropped from this phase by ADR-001 and waiting on the operator: waits on T031, moved to the packet's operator list by ADR-001. Original task: Only when T031's rollout contains the brief: in `briefDelivered` (`OF`), decide `codex` from its raw rollout in the shape T031 shows, with one `OT` case built from that shape. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed. When T031's rollout holds no brief, mark this task `[x]` with `Dropped: no Codex brief in the smoke rollout`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:140:- [x] All tasks marked `[x]`, with T024 to T026 and T032 either done or marked dropped with their measured reason. Evidence: T024 to T026 are dropped on the measured cold-start numbers, and T031 and T032 are dropped from this phase by ADR-001 and sit on the packet's operator list\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/decision-record.md:3