ecting `true`, and `it.each([['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:agent'], ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete', '/speckit:plan'], ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:plan'], ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:implement'], ['do not run /speckit:complete or run /speckit:plan', '/speckit:plan']])('still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list', ...)` expecting `false`. In the table of the case `offers no hub command for %s`, add the row `'do not run /create:agent or /create:readme'`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the five refusal rows and the hub row fail while the six request rows pass. Then in `CA`, directly below `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`, add ``const COMMAND_OR_LIST = '(?:\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?,? or )*';`` with a comment saying a refusal over an or-list refuses every command the list joins to the one its lead names, while a second use verb opens a clause of its own, so the list joins only `or` and `, or`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, replace the `const led = [...COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS, ...COMMAND_ASK_LEADS].some(...)` statement with one that tests each decline lead as ``new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`)`` and each ask lead as it is tested now. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c 'COMMAND_OR_LIST' $CA` prints 2, `TC` exits 0 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 6 failed of 131 (the five or-list refusals and the hub row), then 131 of 131. typecheck 0, COMMAND_OR_LIST count 2, mention probe 46 of 46. Requests after an or-list refusal still keep their command\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/containment/baseline/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:121:- [x] T020 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). After T019. Run the commands of T002 in the same order and write each with its output. Verify: `rg -e '^(do not run /create:agent or|never use /create:readme or|do not run /deep:review, or)' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -e '\"/(create:(readme|feature-catalog|agent)|deep:(review|research))\"'` prints nothing. `rg -e '^Is the /doctor:update' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -F '\"/doctor:update\"'` prints nothing. The lines for `use /create:agent or /create:readme`, `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` and `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README`, and both `ROUTE` lines, equal their lines in `repro-before.txt`. Every `heredoc` line ends in `improvised`, the `shellRead startState` line reads `{\"started\":true,\"unsafe\":false,\"selfAuto\":false}`, `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]`, the `OFFERS` count prints 9 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. When the `OFFERS` count differs, list the changed lines from its review-authored prompt file, and the task holds when each is a refusal over an or-list or an `is the` question. Any other difference marks the task `[B]` with the line. Evidence: repro-after.txt: the three or-list refusals and the Is the question carry no command, the request lines, the README statement and both ROUTE lines equal before, every heredoc improvised, shellRead started true, HAS offeredAs, APPROVED-FILE, OFFERS 9, MENTION 46 of 46\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/containment/baseline/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:139:- [ ] `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints no refused command on the three or-list refusal lines and holds `HAS offeredAs`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md:33:that a refusal over an or-list and an is-the question carry no command while a request over a\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:9:- Sources read: `review-brief-4.txt:1`, `review-scope-4.txt:6-9`, `_routes.yaml:1-828` (mutation classes and phrases), `command-bridges.generated.json` (policy rows queried as data), `derive-command-bridges.cjs:470-539,710-777`, `command-attach.ts:445-519`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1-269`, `doctor-command-routing.md:13-82`, `doctor-setup-run.md:1-110`, `doctor-update-check.md:1-109`, `016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md:44-56,169,250-280,354`, `016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/acceptance-criteria.md:58-62`, `016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md:92-133`, `024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md:111-112`, `024-fable-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:92`, the `a494145dd0` commit body, and the runtime mirror listing for `.claude`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.pi`, `.dsh`, `.devin`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-001.md:108:- The published routing baseline contains no per-row holdout outcome in any of its maps or lists.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md:42:- [ ] D1 Correctness — new or-list grammar in `commandOnlyMentioned`, refusal/question/request split\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md:16:The CLI front door `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` is the only surface over the advisor daemon contract. The CLI exposes 9 commands through a hand-maintained manifest whose schemas are held byte-identical to the server `TOOL_DEFINITIONS` by a dedicated parity suite (`tests/skill-advisor-cli-manifest-parity.vitest.ts`) — drift between the two registries fails tests rather than shipping. `skill-advisor list-tools --format json` returns `{ status: \"ok\", data: { count: 9 } }` as the runtime parity check. The Python facade `skill_advisor.py` stayed untouched, and the OpenCode plugin plus the Claude/OpenCode prompt-submit hooks shell out to the CLI.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v0.18.1.0.md:3:description: \"A show or list question about the decision-capture queue, a chat candidate or the decision record now routes to spec-kit instead of nowhere, and a request to research or build something about decisions is left alone.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/tar/README.md:343:to extract or list, so they're equivalent to a filter that tests if\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/023-untuned-outcome-evidence/tasks.md:80:- [x] T017 Count the fit rows apart from every other tally (`$CRS`, then `$CAP` function `headCarriesCommand` and the row loop of `scoreCommandCorpus`). After T005. Test first: add the case `counts the sealed fit rows and publishes none`, which asserts `live.attachedMetrics.fit.skillOnly.total` is 24, `fit.decline.total` is 24, each of the four `fit.decline.byKind` totals is 6, every `carried` is at most its `total`, and no key of `live.rows`, `attachedMetrics.attachedRows` or `attachedMetrics.typedRows` starts with `fit-`. It fails because `fit` is undefined. Then add `headCarriesCommand(landed, delivered)`, true when `landed[0]` is not null or `delivered` is defined. In the row loop of `scoreCommandCorpus`, once `delivered` is known, a row whose `row_type` is `skill-only` or `decline` adds 1 to the `total` of its `fit` tally, adds 1 to `carried` when `headCarriesCommand` is true, and continues to the next row, so it takes part in no other count, row map or list. Place that `continue` above the block that counts bridge agreement, so `metrics.agreement` does not count a fit row. A `decline` row also adds to the `byKind` entry named by its `decline_kind`. Publish `attachedMetrics.fit` as `{ skillOnly: { carried, total }, decline: { carried, total, byKind } }`. Verify: `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` reports the new case failed before the change and passes after it, the case `publishes no holdout row` passes, and only the `attachedMetrics` and corpus hash comparisons fail until T006. Evidence: Opus check PASS: first run cannot destructure skillOnly (3 failed), after a dist rebuild 2 failed of 9, attachedMetrics and the corpus hash, both cleared by the T006 recapture. publishes no holdout row passes, typecheck exit 0\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:70:- [x] T003 [P] Count a shell read of a workflow document as a load (`S`, `CTS`). Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('workflowPath')`, add `it('counts a shell read of the owner entry document as a skill load')` expecting `workflowPath([ev(0, 'shell', { command: 'cat .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md' })], { command: '/create:agent', owner: 'sk-doc', wrote: false })` to be `'skill'`, `it('counts a shell read of the command document as a command load')` expecting `workflowPath([ev(0, 'shell', { command: 'sed -n 1,80p .opencode/commands/create/agent.md | head -40' }), ev(1, 'write', { path: '.opencode/agents/x.md' })], { command: '/create:agent', owner: 'sk-doc', wrote: true })` to be `'command'`, and `it.each(['echo .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md', 'ls .skilled/skills/sk-doc', 'cat notes.md > .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md'])('does not count %s as a load', ...)` expecting `'none'` for the first two and a value other than `'skill'` for the third. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the first two cases return `'none'` and `'improvised'`. Then in `S`, above `followedBeforeWrite`, add `const SHELL_READERS = Object.freeze(['cat', 'head', 'tail', 'sed', 'less', 'more', 'bat', 'nl', 'awk', 'rg', 'grep'])` and `function shellReadTargets(command)`, which splits the command on `;`, `&&`, `||`, `|` and line breaks, keeps each part whose first word, or first word after leading `NAME=value` words, is in `SHELL_READERS`, drops every word that follows a `>` or `>>` operator, strips one pair of surrounding quotes from each remaining word and returns the words that end in `.md`, `.yaml` or `.yml`. Give it a comment saying some runtimes read a document through the shell rather than a read tool, and that only a command that reads a file names one, so a path that is merely printed or listed is not a load. In `followedBeforeWrite`, let a `shell` event through the kind check and build `named` from `shellReadTargets(event.command)` for it. In `ownerLoadedBeforeWrite`, before the compiled-route check, return `true` for a `shell` event before the boundary when one of `shellReadTargets(command)` matches `documents`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run Tests 2 failed, 85 passed (87), expected none to be skill. Passing run Tests 87 passed (87). Opus check PASS, typecheck exit 0, scratch/verify report.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/tasks.md:81:- [x] T010 State the body rule in the reader README (`SRR`). After T009. In the paragraph or list that describes what a record holds, or directly below the table row for `codex.mjs` when no such paragraph exists, add this sentence word for word: ``A Codex custom tool call has no JSON arguments, so its record carries the call's body as `arguments.input`, a string.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'carries the call' $SRR` prints 1 and `rg -c -e '—|;' $SRR` prints the count it printed before the edit. Evidence: Opus check PASS: sentence word for word at README line 32, rg carries the call prints 1, em dash and semicolon count 0 before and after\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:283:| Review pass four verification, 2026-11-14 | 3 P1 and 15 P2 confirmed, 3 rejected | Opus verifier, report review/verify-4/report.md. P1: refusal over an or-list keeps the second command (SA4-P1-002), offeredAs dropped by both run-log writers, a shell read of a command document is not a start (raised from P2). fanout-merge counts 10 active P1 because it merges all 18 lineages of every pass |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:104:| Move T031 and T032 to the packet's operator list (ADR-001) | Approving Codex hooks writes the operator's own `~/.codex/config.toml`. Taken autonomously under the goal's rule D1, not by the operator |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:160:| T031 runs one Codex smoke row after operator approval, and T032 decodes its brief | Both `[B]`, moved to the packet's operator list by ADR-001 | Approval writes the operator's `~/.codex/config.toml` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:129:- [x] T031 [C] Dropped from this phase by ADR-001 and waiting on the operator: moved to the packet's operator list by ADR-001, because approving Codex hooks writes the operator's `~/.codex/config.toml`. Original task: Codex smoke: prepare one arena at this phase's commit, have the operator open `/hooks` in a Codex session there and approve each entry, then run one row through `R` with `--runtime codex --arm smoke`.