five refusal rows and the hub row fail while the six request rows pass. Then in `CA`, directly below `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS`, add ``const COMMAND_OR_LIST = '(?:\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?,? or )*';`` with a comment saying a refusal over an or-list refuses every command the list joins to the one its lead names, while a second use verb opens a clause of its own, so the list joins only `or` and `, or`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, replace the `const led = [...COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS, ...COMMAND_ASK_LEADS].some(...)` statement with one that tests each decline lead as ``new RegExp(`(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])${lead}${COMMAND_OR_LIST}${name}$`)`` and each ask lead as it is tested now. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c 'COMMAND_OR_LIST' $CA` prints 2, `TC` exits 0 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 6 failed of 131 (the five or-list refusals and the hub row), then 131 of 131. typecheck 0, COMMAND_OR_LIST count 2, mention probe 46 of 46. Requests after an or-list refusal still keep their command\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/containment/baseline/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:121:- [x] T020 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). After T019. Run the commands of T002 in the same order and write each with its output. Verify: `rg -e '^(do not run /create:agent or|never use /create:readme or|do not run /deep:review, or)' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -e '\"/(create:(readme|feature-catalog|agent)|deep:(review|research))\"'` prints nothing. `rg -e '^Is the /doctor:update' $SP/repro-after.txt | sed 's/.* => //' | rg -c -F '\"/doctor:update\"'` prints nothing. The lines for `use /create:agent or /create:readme`, `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` and `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README`, and both `ROUTE` lines, equal their lines in `repro-before.txt`. Every `heredoc` line ends in `improvised`, the `shellRead startState` line reads `{\"started\":true,\"unsafe\":false,\"selfAuto\":false}`, `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`, `RACE` prints `recordsText [ 'APPROVED-FILE' ]`, the `OFFERS` count prints 9 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. When the `OFFERS` count differs, list the changed lines from its review-authored prompt file, and the task holds when each is a refusal over an or-list or an `is the` question. Any other difference marks the task `[B]` with the line. Evidence: repro-after.txt: the three or-list refusals and the Is the question carry no command, the request lines, the README statement and both ROUTE lines equal before, every heredoc improvised, shellRead started true, HAS offeredAs, APPROVED-FILE, OFFERS 9, MENTION 46 of 46\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/containment/baseline/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:139:- [ ] `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints no refused command on the three or-list refusal lines and holds `HAS offeredAs`\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md:33:that a refusal over an or-list and an is-the question carry no command while a request over a\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/iterations/iteration-002.md:9:- Sources read: `review-brief-4.txt:1`, `review-scope-4.txt:6-9`, `_routes.yaml:1-828` (mutation classes and phrases), `command-bridges.generated.json` (policy rows queried as data), `derive-command-bridges.cjs:470-539,710-777`, `command-attach.ts:445-519`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:1