{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683323203,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7638b1001l7lVOFABAB2jg0","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db7618a9001d0WKLFIhSlEwbD","type":"tool","id":"call_a1fe337bcc8242c1a47956cd","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n -i \"article\\|question over\\|or-list\\|T028\\|T029\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"3:description: \"Review pass four confirmed that a refusal over an or-list still hands over its second command, that neither run-log writer keeps where an offered command sat in the head, and that a shell read of a command document counts as a load but not as a start. This phase fixes those three and nine confirmed P2 findings, test first, rescores every stored arm and restates each moved start figure before phase 026 freezes its stored numbers and runs 864 sessions.\"\n7:  - \"or-list refusal mention reader\"\n51:- A mention reader that reads a refusal over an or-list as a refusal of every command in it, and a question that puts `the` before the command as a question.\n201:| SA4-P1-002, a refusal over an or-list keeps its second command | `commandOnlyMentioned` (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts:405`) needs a lead directly before each naming, and no lead crosses the first command and its `or` | Fix (T004). A decline lead also covers every command an or-list joins to the one it leads. All three callers read the same function, so the typed path, the hub path and the scorer withhold alike. `use A or B` and `use A, not B` keep their commands |\n228:- Read a refusal over an or-list as a refusal of each command in it, and `is the /x command` as a question.\n239:- An or-list joined by `and`, `nor` or a bare comma, and a question over an or-list - no probe reproduced them (P049).\n248:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The or-list carry for the decline leads and `(?:the )?` in the bare ask lead |\n249:| `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | The or-list refusals, their controls and the `the` question rows |\n307:- **SC-001**: The CLI probe prints no row with `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:agent`, `/deep:review` or `/deep:research` for the three or-list refusals, where row 0 printed `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` and `/deep:research`.\n322:| Risk | The or-list carry withholds a real request | Med: a reader who asked for a command loses it | Guard rows for `use A or B`, `use A, not B`, `do not run A, run B or C` and `do not run A or run B`, and the 024 mention probe must still print 46 of 46 |\n356:- Maximum input: an or-list of three or more commands joined by `or` after one decline lead refuses every command in it, as `do not run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement or /speckit:complete` does in T004. A list joined by a bare comma is out of scope (P049).\n384:- A3. The or-list carry joins `or` and `, or` only and applies to the decline leads only (P049). `and`, `nor`, a bare comma and a question over an or-list had no reproduction, which P022 and P024 require before a new rule.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Review pass four confirmed that a refusal over an or-list still hands over its second command, that neither run-log writer keeps where an offered command sat in the head, and that a shell read of a command document counts as a load but not as a start. This phase fixes those three and nine confirmed P2 findings, test first, rescores every stored arm and restates each moved start figure before phase 026 freezes its stored numbers and runs 864 sessions.\"\n7:  - \"or-list refusal mention reader\"\n51:- A mention reader that reads a refusal over an or-list as a refusal of every command in it, and a question that puts `the` before the command as a question.\n201:| SA4-P1-002, a refusal over an or-list keeps its second command | `commandOnlyMentioned` (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts:405`) needs a lead directly before each naming, and no lead crosses the first command and its `or` | Fix (T004). A decline lead also covers every command an or-list joins to the one it leads. All three callers read the same function, so the typed path, the hub path and the scorer withhold alike. `use A or B` and `use A, not B` keep their commands |\n228:- Read a refusal over an or-list as a refusal of each command in it, and `is the /x command` as a question.\n239:- An or-list joined by `and`, `nor` or a bare comma, and a question over an or-list - no probe reproduced them (P049).\n248:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The or-list carry for the decline leads and `(?:the )?` in the bare ask lead |\n249:| `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | The or-list refusals, their controls and the `the` question rows |\n307:- **SC-001**: The CLI probe prints no row with `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:agent`, `/deep:review` or `/deep:research` for the three or-list refusals, where row 0 printed `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` and `/deep:research`.\n322:| Risk | The or-list carry withholds a real request | Med: a reader who asked for a command loses it | Guard rows for `use A or B`, `use A, not B`, `do not run A, run B or C` and `do not run A or run B`, and the 024 mention probe must still print 46 of 46 |\n356:- Maximum input: an or-list of three or more commands joined by `or` after one decline lead refuses every command in it, as `do not run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement or /speckit:complete` does in T004. A list joined by a bare comma is out of scope (P049).\n384:- A3. The or-list carry joins `or` and `, or` only and applies to the decline leads only (P049). `and`, `nor`, a bare comma and a question over an or-list had no reproduction, which P022 and P024 require before a new rule.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n -i \\\"article\\\\|question over\\\\|or-list\\\\|T028\\\\|T029\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683320497,"end":1794683323203}}}}
