{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683390994,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db774437002vKKlwFGQsUHZck","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db77344b001FXOOG48ieGYRyX","type":"tool","id":"call_a760bba06ee243c3b26abd03","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '432,465p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"      data: upcast.data,\n      prevEventHash: upcast.prevEventHash,\n      replay: upcast.replay,\n    }, upcast.occurredAt ? { occurredAt: upcast.occurredAt, ...rawEvent } : rawEvent);\n    eventRecord = adapter.prepareEvent(preparedInput, registry);\n    legacyWarnings = upcast.warnings;\n  } else if (\n    normalizedMode === 'deep-review'\n    && rawEvent\n    && typeof rawEvent === 'object'\n    && !Array.isArray(rawEvent)\n    && rawEvent.type === 'iteration'\n  ) {\n    // The review agent, its iteration prompt and its workflow all hand the gateway the canonical\n    // iteration record itself. Its optional fields vary with review depth and executor, so it\n    // travels whole under one stem, and the state projection writes it back as the same row.\n    const sessionId = typeof rawEvent.sessionId === 'string' && rawEvent.sessionId\n      ? rawEvent.sessionId\n      : 'run-cli';\n    const preparedInput = buildPreparedInput({\n      stem: 'deep_review.iteration_recorded',\n      scope: { runId: sessionId, sessionId },\n      data: { record: rawEvent },\n      prevEventHash: currentHead.recordHash,\n      replay: defaultReplay,\n    }, rawEvent);\n    eventRecord = adapter.prepareEvent(preparedInput, registry);\n  } else {\n    throw new Error('Unrecognized event format: expected object with stem or event_type');\n  }\n\n  const outcome = await appendModeEvent({\n    mode: normalizedMode,\n    runDirectory,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      data: upcast.data,\n      prevEventHash: upcast.prevEventHash,\n      replay: upcast.replay,\n    }, upcast.occurredAt ? { occurredAt: upcast.occurredAt, ...rawEvent } : rawEvent);\n    eventRecord = adapter.prepareEvent(preparedInput, registry);\n    legacyWarnings = upcast.warnings;\n  } else if (\n    normalizedMode === 'deep-review'\n    && rawEvent\n    && typeof rawEvent === 'object'\n    && !Array.isArray(rawEvent)\n    && rawEvent.type === 'iteration'\n  ) {\n    // The review agent, its iteration prompt and its workflow all hand the gateway the canonical\n    // iteration record itself. Its optional fields vary with review depth and executor, so it\n    // travels whole under one stem, and the state projection writes it back as the same row.\n    const sessionId = typeof rawEvent.sessionId === 'string' && rawEvent.sessionId\n      ? rawEvent.sessionId\n      : 'run-cli';\n    const preparedInput = buildPreparedInput({\n      stem: 'deep_review.iteration_recorded',\n      scope: { runId: sessionId, sessionId },\n      data: { record: rawEvent },\n      prevEventHash: currentHead.recordHash,\n      replay: defaultReplay,\n    }, rawEvent);\n    eventRecord = adapter.prepareEvent(preparedInput, registry);\n  } else {\n    throw new Error('Unrecognized event format: expected object with stem or event_type');\n  }\n\n  const outcome = await appendModeEvent({\n    mode: normalizedMode,\n    runDirectory,\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '432,465p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683388983,"end":1794683390994}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683391001,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7746cd001dfLaYAciqW30wX","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db77344b001FXOOG48ieGYRyX","type":"tool","id":"call_ca337ec603474e698e11c427","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '230,245p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \"===A3===\"; sed -n '378,390p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \"===T025===\"; grep -n \"T025\" -A 4 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md | head -12","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"- Count a shell read of a command document as a start and as a loop the run took, drop heredoc bodies whose end word holds a hyphen or a dot, read the Codex rollout at the resolved path and make the holdout guard read the live capture.\n- Rescore every stored arm, list each newly counted start with its row and the rule that moved it, and restate each moved start figure in superseding goal log rows.\n- Correct five documents, run a confirming review on the scorer-attach and accuracy-runner areas and write the pass-four synthesis.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- A backfill of `offeredAs` onto stored run lines - a replay today prints today's head, not the one the run saw.\n- The README statement gap - it lives in the `sk-doc` route vocabulary, the class P017 names, and a word change to move one review prompt would be tuning on it.\n- SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 - accepted limits of phase 020 (P045).\n- The pair README sentence, the reserved arm name `paired` and the dead `unscoredOnly` count - phase 026 rewrites the same functions (P046).\n- An or-list joined by `and`, `nor` or a bare comma, and a question over an or-list - no probe reproduced them (P049).\n- Any new behaviour run, the release notes and the reference pages phase 025 owns.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `RAD` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy` and `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared`.\n\n===A3===\n<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does a missing `--keep` value delete every archive? Decision: no, a missing value exits 2. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n\nNone blocks planning. The planner could ask the operator nothing, so each point the dispatch left open is decided below and recorded as an assumption, open for the coordinator or the operator to overturn.\n\n- A1. Level: `recommend-level.sh --loc 380 --files 17` printed Level 1. Decision: Level 2, because `acceptance-criteria.md` is the closure gate, as P001 and P025 decided for phases 020 to 026. The plan workflow says to go higher when its answer and judgment differ.\n- A2. The plan ran without `:auto` as a non-interactive worker. Each checkpoint took its first option as the default, and step 7 took Skip, as the workflow's child-dispatch rule says. Step 5's four exploration agents were not dispatched, because this planner may dispatch none, and the same reads were done inline. No `research/research.md` was written, as in phases 024 and 026. Step 6 did not run `generate-context.js`, because the spec authoring card forbids it for a packet author and its writes can reach files outside this phase's write scope.\n- A3. The or-list carry joins `or` and `, or` only and applies to the decline leads only (P049). `and`, `nor`, a bare comma and a question over an or-list had no reproduction, which P022 and P024 require before a new rule.\n- A4. `do not run A or run B` keeps B's command. A second use verb opens a new clause, the way `do not run /x, run /y instead` already reads, and no current rule carries a negation across a verb. A guard row pins the choice (P049).\n- A5. The ungraded README statement is a route vocabulary gap at P2 (P047). The mention fixes cannot reach it, and SA2-P2-002's grounds hold: `start` asks before it writes and Gate 2 lets an explicit instruction outrank the policy.\n- A6. SA4-P2-004 is a superseding note here, not an erratum in phase 020 (P048).\n- A7. The live writer is tested through an exported `offerLineFields`, one helper and its one call (P019).\n- A8. The Codex fix is tested by `trackFileOpens` on a symlink inside the store, the helper the other reader tests use, not by a swap, because `resolveInside` opens nothing and the read path alone shows the defect.\n- A9. The rescore follows phase 024 T021: before files at T003, after files at T021, one delta line per runtime and arm. A per-row list over every row id of each set finds the moved runs, and a copy of the scorer with the shell-read line undone, written outside the repository with absolute imports as the verifier's sed does, attributes each move.\n===T025===\n81:- [x] T028 Carry the article form through the or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its comment). Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P1-001: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still printed `[[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"],...]`. This task changes that one constant and its comment and nothing else in `CA`. The new value is `'(?:(?:the )?\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?: command)?,? or (?:the )?)*'`, so a listed command may carry `the` before it and `command` after it, and the command after the last `or` may carry `the`. Test first: in `CAT`, add four rows to the table of the case `reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list`: `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` and `['never use the /create:readme command or the /create:feature-catalog command', '/create:feature-catalog']`, and one row to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`: `['use /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four refusal rows fail, then change the constant and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 5 more tests than before, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 4 failed of 138, then 138 of 138. Constant matches the task value, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, no wrongly refused command in an edge probe\n82:- [x] T029 Read a question over an or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` function `commandOnlyMentioned` and the comment of `COMMAND_OR_LIST`). After T028. Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P2-001: `should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?` and `is /create:agent or /create:readme better?` each printed `/create:readme` with policy `start`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, insert `${COMMAND_OR_LIST}` directly before `${name}` in the `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` test and in both `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` tests, three insertions and nothing else in the function, and change the first sentence of the comment above `COMMAND_OR_LIST` so it says a refusal or a question over an or-list covers every command the list joins. Test first: in `CAT`, add a table case `reads %s as a question about %s through an or-list` with the rows `['should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?', '/create:readme']`, `['is /create:agent or /create:readme better?', '/create:readme']` and `['what does /create:agent or /create:readme do?', '/create:readme']`, each expecting `commandOnlyMentioned` to return `true`, and add the row `['the next step is /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme']` to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`. Run the file and see the three question rows fail, then make the change and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 3 failed of 142, then 142 of 142. Three insertions of COMMAND_OR_LIST, comment reworded, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, a later unled request and a mid-sentence is still read as requests\n83-\n84-### Lane O: the two run-log writers\n85-\n86-- [x] T006 [P] Keep `offeredAs` on a backfilled line (`COT`, then `CO` function `backfillRunLog`). After T003. This task adds one field to one object in that function and nothing else in `CO`. Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head')`, built as the case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once` builds its two lines, whose `replay` returns `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null }` when `sessionId` is `backfill-row-one` and `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }` otherwise, and which expects the first written line's `offeredAs` to be `'partner'` and the second's to be `null`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see `offeredAs` read `undefined`. Then in the `else` branch that builds `nextLine`, directly after `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,`, add `offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: where the command sat in the head travels with it, because a command on the partner side was shown and not offered. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `recomputes only the brief when the offers are already recorded` still passes, `node --check $CO` exits 0 and `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 30 (expected undefined to be partner), then 30 of 30. BACKFILL prints HAS offeredAs, node --check 0, typecheck 0\n--\n106:- [x] T030 Count the four fields in every sentence and name the line that carries none (`RA`). After T013. Added by T025 after the confirming round found AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002. In the sentence that starts `` `run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields``, replace `three fields` with `four fields`. In the runner's row, replace ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` `` with ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered` ``. Directly after the line `Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:` and its list, at the end of the `briefDelivered` item, add the sentence `A line written when the head moved stops before the offer is read, so it carries none of the four and holds headMoved instead.` Verify: `rg -c 'three fields' $RAD/README.md` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'carries none of the four' $RAD/README.md` prints 1 and `rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`' $RAD/README.md` prints 1. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three edits, rg three fields prints nothing, the other two rg checks print 1, the head-moved sentence matches the code\n107-\n108-### Lane E: four documents\n109-\n110-- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'A hub below the head leaves' $FA` prints 1, and `rg -n -F 'index === 0' $ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` prints one line. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact two-sentence replacement, both rg counts 1, index === 0 at advisor-recommend.ts:478\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- Count a shell read of a command document as a start and as a loop the run took, drop heredoc bodies whose end word holds a hyphen or a dot, read the Codex rollout at the resolved path and make the holdout guard read the live capture.\n- Rescore every stored arm, list each newly counted start with its row and the rule that moved it, and restate each moved start figure in superseding goal log rows.\n- Correct five documents, run a confirming review on the scorer-attach and accuracy-runner areas and write the pass-four synthesis.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- A backfill of `offeredAs` onto stored run lines - a replay today prints today's head, not the one the run saw.\n- The README statement gap - it lives in the `sk-doc` route vocabulary, the class P017 names, and a word change to move one review prompt would be tuning on it.\n- SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 - accepted limits of phase 020 (P045).\n- The pair README sentence, the reserved arm name `paired` and the dead `unscoredOnly` count - phase 026 rewrites the same functions (P046).\n- An or-list joined by `and`, `nor` or a bare comma, and a question over an or-list - no probe reproduced them (P049).\n- Any new behaviour run, the release notes and the reference pages phase 025 owns.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `RAD` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy` and `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared`.\n\n===A3===\n<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does a missing `--keep` value delete every archive? Decision: no, a missing value exits 2. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n\nNone blocks planning. The planner could ask the operator nothing, so each point the dispatch left open is decided below and recorded as an assumption, open for the coordinator or the operator to overturn.\n\n- A1. Level: `recommend-level.sh --loc 380 --files 17` printed Level 1. Decision: Level 2, because `acceptance-criteria.md` is the closure gate, as P001 and P025 decided for phases 020 to 026. The plan workflow says to go higher when its answer and judgment differ.\n- A2. The plan ran without `:auto` as a non-interactive worker. Each checkpoint took its first option as the default, and step 7 took Skip, as the workflow's child-dispatch rule says. Step 5's four exploration agents were not dispatched, because this planner may dispatch none, and the same reads were done inline. No `research/research.md` was written, as in phases 024 and 026. Step 6 did not run `generate-context.js`, because the spec authoring card forbids it for a packet author and its writes can reach files outside this phase's write scope.\n- A3. The or-list carry joins `or` and `, or` only and applies to the decline leads only (P049). `and`, `nor`, a bare comma and a question over an or-list had no reproduction, which P022 and P024 require before a new rule.\n- A4. `do not run A or run B` keeps B's command. A second use verb opens a new clause, the way `do not run /x, run /y instead` already reads, and no current rule carries a negation across a verb. A guard row pins the choice (P049).\n- A5. The ungraded README statement is a route vocabulary gap at P2 (P047). The mention fixes cannot reach it, and SA2-P2-002's grounds hold: `start` asks before it writes and Gate 2 lets an explicit instruction outrank the policy.\n- A6. SA4-P2-004 is a superseding note here, not an erratum in phase 020 (P048).\n- A7. The live writer is tested through an exported `offerLineFields`, one helper and its one call (P019).\n- A8. The Codex fix is tested by `trackFileOpens` on a symlink inside the store, the helper the other reader tests use, not by a swap, because `resolveInside` opens nothing and the read path alone shows the defect.\n- A9. The rescore follows phase 024 T021: before files at T003, after files at T021, one delta line per runtime and arm. A per-row list over every row id of each set finds the moved runs, and a copy of the scorer with the shell-read line undone, written outside the repository with absolute imports as the verifier's sed does, attributes each move.\n===T025===\n81:- [x] T028 Carry the article form through the or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its comment). Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P1-001: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still printed `[[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"],...]`. This task changes that one constant and its comment and nothing else in `CA`. The new value is `'(?:(?:the )?\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?: command)?,? or (?:the )?)*'`, so a listed command may carry `the` before it and `command` after it, and the command after the last `or` may carry `the`. Test first: in `CAT`, add four rows to the table of the case `reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list`: `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` and `['never use the /create:readme command or the /create:feature-catalog command', '/create:feature-catalog']`, and one row to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`: `['use /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four refusal rows fail, then change the constant and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 5 more tests than before, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 4 failed of 138, then 138 of 138. Constant matches the task value, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, no wrongly refused command in an edge probe\n82:- [x] T029 Read a question over an or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` function `commandOnlyMentioned` and the comment of `COMMAND_OR_LIST`). After T028. Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P2-001: `should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?` and `is /create:agent or /create:readme better?` each printed `/create:readme` with policy `start`. In `commandOnlyMentioned`, insert `${COMMAND_OR_LIST}` directly before `${name}` in the `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` test and in both `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` tests, three insertions and nothing else in the function, and change the first sentence of the comment above `COMMAND_OR_LIST` so it says a refusal or a question over an or-list covers every command the list joins. Test first: in `CAT`, add a table case `reads %s as a question about %s through an or-list` with the rows `['should I run /create:agent or /create:readme?', '/create:readme']`, `['is /create:agent or /create:readme better?', '/create:readme']` and `['what does /create:agent or /create:readme do?', '/create:readme']`, each expecting `commandOnlyMentioned` to return `true`, and add the row `['the next step is /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme']` to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`. Run the file and see the three question rows fail, then make the change and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 3 failed of 142, then 142 of 142. Three insertions of COMMAND_OR_LIST, comment reworded, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, a later unled request and a mid-sentence is still read as requests\n83-\n84-### Lane O: the two run-log writers\n85-\n86-- [x] T006 [P] Keep `offeredAs` on a backfilled line (`COT`, then `CO` function `backfillRunLog`). After T003. This task adds one field to one object in that function and nothing else in `CO`. Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('keeps where the offered command sat in the head')`, built as the case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once` builds its two lines, whose `replay` returns `{ offeredCommand: '/create:manual-testing-playbook', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner', offerError: null }` when `sessionId` is `backfill-row-one` and `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_head' }` otherwise, and which expects the first written line's `offeredAs` to be `'partner'` and the second's to be `null`. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see `offeredAs` read `undefined`. Then in the `else` branch that builds `nextLine`, directly after `offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,`, add `offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,`, and add to the comment above it one sentence: where the command sat in the head travels with it, because a command on the partner side was shown and not offered. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, the case `recomputes only the brief when the offers are already recorded` still passes, `node --check $CO` exits 0 and `BACKFILL` prints `HAS offeredAs`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 30 (expected undefined to be partner), then 30 of 30. BACKFILL prints HAS offeredAs, node --check 0, typecheck 0\n--\n106:- [x] T030 Count the four fields in every sentence and name the line that carries none (`RA`). After T013. Added by T025 after the confirming round found AR4B-P2-001 and AR4B-P2-002. In the sentence that starts `` `run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields``, replace `three fields` with `four fields`. In the runner's row, replace ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` `` with ``rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered` ``. Directly after the line `Each line a behaviour run appends carries four fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:` and its list, at the end of the `briefDelivered` item, add the sentence `A line written when the head moved stops before the offer is read, so it carries none of the four and holds headMoved instead.` Verify: `rg -c 'three fields' $RAD/README.md` prints nothing, `rg -c -F 'carries none of the four' $RAD/README.md` prints 1 and `rg -c -F '`offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs` and `briefDelivered`' $RAD/README.md` prints 1. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: three edits, rg three fields prints nothing, the other two rg checks print 1, the head-moved sentence matches the code\n107-\n108-### Lane E: four documents\n109-\n110-- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'A hub below the head leaves' $FA` prints 1, and `rg -n -F 'index === 0' $ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` prints one line. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact two-sentence replacement, both rg counts 1, index === 0 at advisor-recommend.ts:478\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '230,245p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \\\"===A3===\\\"; sed -n '378,390p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \\\"===T025===\\\"; grep -n \\\"T025\\\" -A 4 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md | head -12\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683389645,"end":1794683391001}}}}
