{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683472775,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db786101001TftmvdXcZLba97","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db7830a7001GVZ9MErHu3F6RV","type":"tool","id":"call_e664b4ce681a468f923f769c","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Importing the real `command-attach.ts` through Node's type stripping and probing the predicate, `attachCommand` and `typedCommandForTop` in one run separated the fixed single-word rows from the failing two-word row (iteration 1).\n- Running the advisor CLI on the same prompts turned the predicate result into a user-visible row list, which confirmed the fix and the remaining hole without touching the corpus (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the diff alone would have missed the multi-word item: the constant looks complete until it is probed with a `/doctor:` command (iteration 1).\n- Extrapolating from the three REQ-001 refusals to \"every command the list joins\" is unsound; the reachable vocabulary decides (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -89,15 +89,17 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Importing the real `command-attach.ts` through Node's type stripping and probing the predicate, `attachCommand` and `typedCommandForTop` in one run separated the fixed single-word rows from the failing two-word row (iteration 1).\n+- Running the advisor CLI on the same prompts turned the predicate result into a user-visible row list, which confirmed the fix and the remaining hole without touching the corpus (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the diff alone would have missed the multi-word item: the constant looks complete until it is probed with a `/doctor:` command (iteration 1).\n+- Extrapolating from the three REQ-001 refusals to \"every command the list joins\" is unsound; the reachable vocabulary decides (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Importing the real `command-attach.ts` through Node's type stripping and probing the predicate, `attachCommand` and `typedCommandForTop` in one run separated the fixed single-word rows from the failing two-word row (iteration 1).\\n- Running the advisor CLI on the same prompts turned the predicate result into a user-visible row list, which confirmed the fix and the remaining hole without touching the corpus (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Reading the diff alone would have missed the multi-word item: the constant looks complete until it is probed with a `/doctor:` command (iteration 1).\\n- Extrapolating from the three REQ-001 refusals to \\\"every command the list joins\\\" is unsound; the reachable vocabulary decides (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683461889,"end":1794683472775}}}}
