{"type":"text","timestamp":1794683571223,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"id":"prt_1db79fea20023H1GD7uoLI1Qoi","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db79a560001LVrFEG4i9N6XWf","type":"text","text":"Iteration 2 (traceability): checking doc claims and the stale pointers.","time":{"start":1794683567778,"end":1794683571223}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683571284,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7a06760019uVmmE8nM6s7aX","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db79a560001LVrFEG4i9N6XWf","type":"tool","id":"call_ca62d83fad6a44c0ac3b1287","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '195,205p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \"===FILES TABLE===\"; sed -n '244,252p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \"===T005===\"; grep -n \"T005\" -A 2 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md | head -6","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"### Mechanism per Finding\n\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` and `RAD` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`.\n\n| Finding | Where it comes from | Decision |\n|---------|---------------------|----------|\n| SA4-P1-002, a refusal over an or-list keeps its second command | `commandOnlyMentioned` (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts:405`) needs a lead directly before each naming, and no lead crosses the first command and its `or` | Fix (T004). A decline lead also covers every command an or-list joins to the one it leads. All three callers read the same function, so the typed path, the hub path and the scorer withhold alike. `use A or B` and `use A, not B` keep their commands |\n| SA4-P2-001, `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` keeps the command | `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` (`:389`) holds no `the` | Fix (T005), `(?:the )?` after the bare ask word |\n| Ungraded, `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` | The `sk-doc` compiled route reads any README statement as `sk-create-readme`, the second probe above, and the head takes that route's command. The mention reader never sees `/create:readme` | Not fixed here. Recorded as a route vocabulary gap at P2 (P047) |\n| iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | `backfillRunLog` (`RAD/command-offer.mjs:490-497`) and `runTurn` (`RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187`) copy the offer's command and policy and drop `offeredAs` | Fix (T006, T007). Stored lines get no backfill, because the head a stored run saw cannot be replayed from today's code |\n| iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start, raised to P1 | `readDocument` (`RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs:913`) reads `read` and `skill` events only, and `startState` and `takenLoop` both call it | Fix (T009). A shell read counts by the rule the load already uses. Every stored arm is rescored (T021) |\n===FILES TABLE===\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `RAD` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy` and `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared`.\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The or-list carry for the decline leads and `(?:the )?` in the bare ask lead |\n| `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | The or-list refusals, their controls and the `the` question rows |\n| `RAD/command-offer.mjs` | Modify | `backfillRunLog` writes `offeredAs` |\n| `ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` | Modify | Two backfill cases |\n| `RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Modify | `offerLineFields` and its one call in `runTurn` |\n===T005===\n57:Worker lanes. Lane A owns `CA` and `CAT` and runs T004 and T005 in order. Lane O owns `CO`, `COT`, `R` and `CBG` and runs T006 and T007 in order. Lane S owns `S` and `CTS` and runs T008 and T009 in order. Lane R owns `CR` and `CRT` and runs T010. Lane T owns `SL` and runs T011. Lane E owns `FA`, `FM`, `AR` and `DP` and runs T014 to T017 in order. These six lanes share no file and run in parallel after T003. Lane D owns `RA` and runs T012 after T007, then T013 after T009. `[P]` marks the first task of lanes A, O, S, R, T and E. Every other task waits for the task before it in its lane. Every lane task is built by DeepSeek v4.1 flash max on OpenCode Go, one task per session, and checked by an Opus verifier before the next task in its lane.\n58-<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n59-\n--\n80:- [x] T005 Read the article after a bare ask word (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD`). After T004. This task changes that one constant and its comment. Test first: in `CAT`, add the row `['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update']` to the table of the case `reads %s as a question about %s`, and the row `['the next step is the /speckit:implement command', '/speckit:implement']` to the table that holds `the next step is /speckit:implement`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first row return `false` while the second passes. Then change `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` to `'(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?'` and add one sentence to the comment above it: a question often names the command after `the`, as in `is the /x command safe`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F \"(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?\" $CA` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 133 (Is the /doctor:update command safe?), then 133 of 133. typecheck 0, mention probe 46 of 46\n81-- [x] T028 Carry the article form through the or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its comment). Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P1-001: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still printed `[[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"],...]`. This task changes that one constant and its comment and nothing else in `CA`. The new value is `'(?:(?:the )?\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?: command)?,? or (?:the )?)*'`, so a listed command may carry `the` before it and `command` after it, and the command after the last `or` may carry `the`. Test first: in `CAT`, add four rows to the table of the case `reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list`: `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` and `['never use the /create:readme command or the /create:feature-catalog command', '/create:feature-catalog']`, and one row to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`: `['use /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four refusal rows fail, then change the constant and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 5 more tests than before, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 4 failed of 138, then 138 of 138. Constant matches the task value, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, no wrongly refused command in an edge probe\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Mechanism per Finding\n\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` and `RAD` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`.\n\n| Finding | Where it comes from | Decision |\n|---------|---------------------|----------|\n| SA4-P1-002, a refusal over an or-list keeps its second command | `commandOnlyMentioned` (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts:405`) needs a lead directly before each naming, and no lead crosses the first command and its `or` | Fix (T004). A decline lead also covers every command an or-list joins to the one it leads. All three callers read the same function, so the typed path, the hub path and the scorer withhold alike. `use A or B` and `use A, not B` keep their commands |\n| SA4-P2-001, `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` keeps the command | `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` (`:389`) holds no `the` | Fix (T005), `(?:the )?` after the bare ask word |\n| Ungraded, `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` | The `sk-doc` compiled route reads any README statement as `sk-create-readme`, the second probe above, and the head takes that route's command. The mention reader never sees `/create:readme` | Not fixed here. Recorded as a route vocabulary gap at P2 (P047) |\n| iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | `backfillRunLog` (`RAD/command-offer.mjs:490-497`) and `runTurn` (`RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1183-1187`) copy the offer's command and policy and drop `offeredAs` | Fix (T006, T007). Stored lines get no backfill, because the head a stored run saw cannot be replayed from today's code |\n| iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start, raised to P1 | `readDocument` (`RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs:913`) reads `read` and `skill` events only, and `startState` and `takenLoop` both call it | Fix (T009). A shell read counts by the rule the load already uses. Every stored arm is rescored (T021) |\n===FILES TABLE===\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `RAD` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy` and `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared`.\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | The or-list carry for the decline leads and `(?:the )?` in the bare ask lead |\n| `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | The or-list refusals, their controls and the `the` question rows |\n| `RAD/command-offer.mjs` | Modify | `backfillRunLog` writes `offeredAs` |\n| `ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` | Modify | Two backfill cases |\n| `RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Modify | `offerLineFields` and its one call in `runTurn` |\n===T005===\n57:Worker lanes. Lane A owns `CA` and `CAT` and runs T004 and T005 in order. Lane O owns `CO`, `COT`, `R` and `CBG` and runs T006 and T007 in order. Lane S owns `S` and `CTS` and runs T008 and T009 in order. Lane R owns `CR` and `CRT` and runs T010. Lane T owns `SL` and runs T011. Lane E owns `FA`, `FM`, `AR` and `DP` and runs T014 to T017 in order. These six lanes share no file and run in parallel after T003. Lane D owns `RA` and runs T012 after T007, then T013 after T009. `[P]` marks the first task of lanes A, O, S, R, T and E. Every other task waits for the task before it in its lane. Every lane task is built by DeepSeek v4.1 flash max on OpenCode Go, one task per session, and checked by an Opus verifier before the next task in its lane.\n58-<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n59-\n--\n80:- [x] T005 Read the article after a bare ask word (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD`). After T004. This task changes that one constant and its comment. Test first: in `CAT`, add the row `['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update']` to the table of the case `reads %s as a question about %s`, and the row `['the next step is the /speckit:implement command', '/speckit:implement']` to the table that holds `the next step is /speckit:implement`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first row return `false` while the second passes. Then change `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` to `'(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?'` and add one sentence to the comment above it: a question often names the command after `the`, as in `is the /x command safe`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F \"(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?\" $CA` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `MENTION` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 1 failed of 133 (Is the /doctor:update command safe?), then 133 of 133. typecheck 0, mention probe 46 of 46\n81-- [x] T028 Carry the article form through the or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its comment). Added by T025 after the confirming round reproduced SAC4B-P1-001: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still printed `[[\"sk-doc\",\"/create:readme\",\"start\"],...]`. This task changes that one constant and its comment and nothing else in `CA`. The new value is `'(?:(?:the )?\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?(?: command)?,? or (?:the )?)*'`, so a listed command may carry `the` before it and `command` after it, and the command after the last `or` may carry `the`. Test first: in `CAT`, add four rows to the table of the case `reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list`: `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`, `['skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` and `['never use the /create:readme command or the /create:feature-catalog command', '/create:feature-catalog']`, and one row to the table of the case `still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list`: `['use /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four refusal rows fail, then change the constant and see the file pass. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with 5 more tests than before, `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0 and `MENTION | tail -2` prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS: worker first run 4 failed of 138, then 138 of 138. Constant matches the task value, typecheck 0, MENTION 46 of 46, no wrongly refused command in an edge probe\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '195,205p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \\\"===FILES TABLE===\\\"; sed -n '244,252p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md; echo \\\"===T005===\\\"; grep -n \\\"T005\\\" -A 2 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md | head -6\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683569782,"end":1794683571284}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683571308,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db79ff9f0011tqNUckbT6im4A","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db79a560001LVrFEG4i9N6XWf","type":"tool","id":"call_1d07a2b2cdcc420cb177e671","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn -i \"mention\\|only names\\|refers to a command\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md | head -20; echo \"===OLD LINE===\"; git show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | grep -n \"export function commandOnlyMentioned\"; git show 11af224a34:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | grep -n \"export function commandOnlyMentioned\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n===OLD LINE===\n411:export function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n405:export function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n===OLD LINE===\n411:export function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n405:export function commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn -i \\\"mention\\\\|only names\\\\|refers to a command\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md | head -20; echo \\\"===OLD LINE===\\\"; git show 48f03b5013:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | grep -n \\\"export function commandOnlyMentioned\\\"; git show 11af224a34:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts | grep -n \\\"export function commandOnlyMentioned\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683568031,"end":1794683571308}}}}
