.","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"error":"Could not find oldString in /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md. It must match exactly, including whitespace and indentation.","metadata":{"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: maintainability with a security cross-reference.\\n- Focus area: the constant's comment against the grammar, the four `${COMMAND_OR_LIST}` insertions, the regex backtracking bound on an untrusted prompt, and whether the two-word gap is visible from the comment or the tests.\\n- Reason: correctness and traceability are covered; the last iteration should close the comment/test maintenance surface and rule the regex out as an input-handling risk before synthesis.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; maintainability final.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: doc-line verification was productive; the real-module probe stays available.\\n- Required evidence: comment lines against regex behaviour, and a bounded-backtracking argument on the repeated-group shape.\\n- Recovery note: none.\",\"oldString\":\"## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: traceability.\\n- Focus area: `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` REQ-001 (`:279`), the Out-of-Scope line (`:239`) and assumption A3 (`:384`) against the code and T029; the shared docs that describe the mention grammar; whether the new forms are pinned at the `attachCommand` layer.\\n- Reason: the predicate and CLI split is confirmed, so the remaining round risk is a document or stored expectation still describing the pre-fix grammar.\\n- Rotat