{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683669988,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7b8bc60010IrAqk85ZKtZy5","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db7b7c34001k1511yKbE1u4Fn","type":"tool","id":"call_c62506b8966d4add893e909b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-230\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-close-4c lineage\n3: description: Runtime strategy tracking the closing round of review pass four for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\n4: version: 1.11.14.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-close-4c lineage\n8: \n9: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n10: \n11: ### Purpose\n12: \n13: Persistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n14: (P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\n15: iteration before any review action.\n16: \n17: ### Ownership\n18: \n19: Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\n20: commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Closing round of review pass four of\n27: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` in the\n28: `scorer-attach` area, over the fix commit range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`.\n29: \n30: Scope: the `scorer-attach` rows of `review/review-scope-4c.txt` — `command-attach.ts` and\n31: `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` — and the shared docs that describe them. The\n32: `accuracy-runner` row (the routing-accuracy `README.md`) belongs to the sibling lineage and is\n33: read here only as doc context. The round confirms the fixes for SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4B-P2-001\n34: and for the verified findings in `review/verify-4/report.md`, and looks for defects the fixes\n35: added. A finding that report rejects, or records as an accepted limit, is not re-raised without\n36: a new input that breaks it.\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n41: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n42: - [ ] security\n43: - [ ] traceability\n44: - [ ] maintainability\n45: \n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n51: \n52: - The accuracy-runner harness, its run-log writers and session readers are the sibling\n53:   lineage's code scope; this lineage checks only that its own scorer surface agrees with them.\n54: - Hook, plugin, render and doctor-command code is outside both scope rows.\n55: - Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n56:   `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n57: - No code changes: review is observation-only.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n62: \n63: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold.\n64: - Cap: `maxIterations` 3; the terminal record must carry `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\n65: - Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n66: - Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n71: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n72: - [x] correctness\n73: \n74: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n79: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n80: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n81: - P1 (Required): 1\n82: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n83: - Resolved: 0\n84: \n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n90: \n91: - Importing the real `command-attach.ts` through Node's type stripping and probing the predicate, `attachCommand` and `typedCommandForTop` in one run separated the fixed single-word rows from the failing two-word row (iteration 1).\n92: - Running the advisor CLI on the same prompts turned the predicate result into a user-visible row list, which confirmed the fix and the remaining hole without touching the corpus (iteration 1).\n93: - Comparing each spec sentence against a `git show` of the prior commit located the stale line pointer and the stale scope text in one pass (iteration 2).\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n98: \n99: - Reading the diff alone would have missed the multi-word item: the constant looks complete until it is probed with a `/doctor:` command (iteration 1).\n100: - Extrapolating from the three REQ-001 refusals to \"every command the list joins\" is unsound; the reachable vocabulary decides (iteration 1).\n101: - Reading the spec's Out-of-Scope line as current scope would have hidden that T029 had already implemented the question carry; the tasks file is the newer record (iteration 2).\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n106: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n107: ### **The article allowance breaks an existing question row**: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` and the sentence-start bare-ask rows still read as questions, because the added group matches zero iterations when no `or` is present. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n108: - What was tried: **The article allowance breaks an existing question row**: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` and the sentence-start bare-ask rows still read as questions, because the added group matches zero iterations when no `or` is present.\n109: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n110: - Do NOT retry: **The article allowance breaks an existing question row**: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` and the sentence-start bare-ask rows still read as 