pproaches -->\n153: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n154: - Completed pivots: 0\n155: - Failed pivots: 0\n156: - Audited overrides: 0\n157: - Swept: none yet\n158: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n159: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n160: \n161: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n162: \n163: [Investigated and eliminated angles are consolidated here from iteration dead-end data]\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n168: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n169: - Dimension: traceability. - Focus area: `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` REQ-001 (`:279`), the Out-of-Scope line (`:239`) and assumption A3 (`:384`) against the code and T029; the shared docs that describe the mention grammar; and whether the new forms are pinned at the `attachCommand` layer as well as at the predicate. - Reason: the fixes are confirmed at the predicate and the CLI, so the remaining risk in this round is a document or a stored expectation that still describes the pre-fix grammar. - Rotation status: correctness complete; traceability next, then maintainability/security. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: correctness probe (real module + CLI) was productive; the same method applies to any doc claim. - Required evidence: exact `file:line` for each doc sentence, and a check of the hub-command table for the new forms. - Recovery note: none. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n170: \n171: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n172: \n173: ---\n174: \n175: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n176: \n177: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n178: \n179: - Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (module under review), `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (its unit tests).\n180: - Behavior claims: a refusal or a question over an or-list carries no command; a request over an or-list keeps its command; the article `the` and the word `command` may appear on a listed item; the command after the last `or` may carry `the`.\n181: - Findings to confirm: SAC4B-P1-001 (a refusal over `A or the B command` kept B), SAC4B-P2-001 (a question over an or-list kept its second command).\n182: - Prior report: `review/verify-4/report.md` — 3 P1 and 15 P2 confirmed, 3 rejected. Rejected and accepted-limit findings are not re-raised without a new input.\n183: - Commands that attach a command live in `MODE_COMMANDS` (`sk-design`, `sk-doc`, `system-deep-loop`); multi-word commands exist only under `/doctor:` and are typed-command rows.\n184: - Conventions: comment explains the grammar it guards; every new rule carries a test row.\n185: - Out-of-scope areas: the run-log writers (`command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`) and the accuracy runner belong to the sibling lineage.\n186: \n187: ---\n188: \n189: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n190: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n191: \n192: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n193: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n194: | `spec_code` | core | partial | 1 | REQ-001's three refusals pass at the CLI; the code comment's \"every command the list joins\" fails for two-word `/doctor:` items |\n195: | `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 1 | T028 and T029 are `[x]` with matching verifier evidence; AC-001 and AC-006 stay `Unmet` until this round closes (AC-011), which is expected |\n196: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no agent surface in this lineage's scope |\n197: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no runtime mirror in this lineage's scope |\n198: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | 0 | [feature-catalog docs to check] |\n199: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | 0 | no playbook surface in this lineage's scope |\n200: \n201: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n202: \n203: ---\n204: \n205: <!-- ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n206: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n207: \n208: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n209: |------|-