{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794683979624,"sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","part":{"partID":"prt_1db7fb1180014I9Uzsb1F0IGaN","sessionID":"ses_e2491b3d5ffeWEHdGsB4TJKTsi","messageID":"msg_1db7f8483001Kh2XKGnMDue9kS","type":"tool","id":"call_ad1efc9c4a684a35945fa704","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report — scorer-attach closing round, pass four\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL**\n- **hasAdvisories: false** (the verdict is CONDITIONAL, not PASS with advisories)\n- **Active findings: 0 P0, 1 P1, 1 P2**\n- **Review scope:** the `scorer-attach` rows of `review-scope-4c.txt` — `command-attach.ts` and `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` — plus the docs that describe them, for commit range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`. Inspection was read-only; all writes are inside `review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/`.\n- **Iterations:** 3 of 3 (cap reached and recorded as `maxIterationsReached`; the last iteration's `newFindingsRatio` was 0.00, below the 0.10 threshold).\n- **Operator review focus (verbatim):**\n\n> Closing round of review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and follow specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4c.txt: it names the scope file, the commit range, which files your lineage reviews and the checks. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n\nThe round's own checks resolve as follows. **Refusals over an or-list** carry no command, with the article and the word `command`, and the plain form, at the predicate, `attachCommand` and the advisor CLI. **Questions over an or-list** carry no command; **requests over a list** keep their command. The exception is a list whose non-final item is a two-word `/doctor:` command, which is the active P1. The `offeredAs`, shell-read, heredoc, Codex-read and live-holdout checks belong to the sibling `accuracy-runner` lineage and to `verify-4`, and were not re-graded here; the docs this lineage read agree with the scorer code.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required: an active P1 remains.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SAC4C-P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word /doctor command still publishes the refused command\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:380\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SAC4C-P2-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The remediation spec still calls the question-over-an-or-list unreproduced and out of scope, and describes the carry as decline-only\",\n      \"file\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:239\",\n      \"dimension\": \"traceability\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-1\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"findingIds\": [\"SAC4C-P1-001\"],\n      \"action\": \"Extend the or-list item grammar to a two-word command, or record the limit; pin both the predicate and the CLI row.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"WS-2\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"findingIds\": [\"SAC4C-P2-001\"],\n      \"action\": \"Amend the remediation spec's requirement, scope, file table and assumption to match the implemented question carry, and correct the moved line pointer.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": \"Record that an or-list refusal or question covers every joined command the tracked table can express, and state whether two-word /doctor commands are in scope. Record the confirming-round additions (article form, question over a list) in the phase requirement rather than only in the appended tasks.\",\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add a test row for `do not run /doctor:ci report or /doctor:ci scaffold` to the or-list refusal table and to the `offers no hub command for %s` table; expect no command on either surface.\",\n    \"Widen `COMMAND_OR_LIST`'s item to an optional second word, or derive the item from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, then re-run the single-word rows, the request rows and the CLI probe.\",\n    \"Amend `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`: REQ-001, the Out-of-Scope line, the Files-to-Change description, A3 and the mechanism pointer (:405 to :412).\",\n    \"Re-run the confirming round over the amended diff; keep the ratio at or below 0.10.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"incomplete-fix\", \"doc-drift\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"commandOnlyMentioned\",\n    \"typedCommandForTop\",\n    \"withholdMentionedCommands\",\n    \"rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst\",\n    \"COMMAND_OR_LIST\",\n    \"advisor CLI rows\",\n    \"027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### SAC4C-P1-001 — P1, correctness\n\n- **Title:** An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word `/doctor:` command still publishes the refused command.\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:380` (applied at `:427`, `:429`, `:432`, `:439`).\n- **Evidence:** `COMMAND_OR_LIST` matches a listed item as one token. `TRACKED_COMMANDS` ships 22 two-word `/doctor:` rows (`:143-178`), and `withholdMentionedCommands` compares a command row on its base name (`fusion.ts:1209`), so the second occurrence is unled. The CLI printed `[[\"command-doctor-ci-report\",\"/doctor:ci report\",\"run\"],[\"command-doctor-ci-scaffold\",\"/doctor:ci scaffold\",\"ask\"]]` for `do not run /doctor:ci report or /doctor:ci scaffold`; `typedCommandForTop('sk-code', …)` returned `/doctor:ci scaffold`. Both were reproduced at synthesis on the final tree.\n- **Impact:** a reader who explicitly refuses two `/doctor:` commands is shown both refused commands on the top two rows, and the typed-command path can attach the refused command. Same symptom class as the SAC4B-P1-001 this round fixed, narrowed to the two-word rows.\n- **Fix recommendation:** let the list item carry an optional second word (`(?: [a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?`), or match the item against the tracked command vocabulary; add the predicate row and a hub/CLI row; keep the request, question and second-use-verb controls green.\n- **Disposition:** active; not a regression introduced by the fix (the pre-fix constant had the same single-token shape), but the fix's own contract sentence claims \"every command the list joins\".\n- **Finding class:** incomplete-fix. **Scope proof:** item pattern at `:380`, call sites at `:427-439`, two-word rows at `:143-178`, base-name comparison at `fusion.ts:1209`. **Affected surface hints:** `commandOnlyMentioned`, `typedCommandForTop`, `withholdMentionedCommands`, `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, `COMMAND_OR_LIST`, advisor CLI rows.\n- **Claim adjudication:** HUNTER found a positional multi-word gap; SKEPTIC checked REQ-001, A3/P049 and the 020 accepted limits and found no recorded exclusion; REFEREE kept P1 because the module's stated contract and a real CLI row reproduce it. Confidence high. Downgrade to P2 only with a recorded single-token or out-of-contract declaration.\n\n### SAC4C-P2-001 — P2, traceability\n\n- **Title:** The remediation spec still calls the question-over-an-or-list unreproduced and out of scope, and describes the carry as decline-only.\n- **File:line:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:239` (also `:201`, `:248`, `:279`, `:384`).\n- **Evidence:** the Out-of-Scope line says a question over an or-list was never reproduced; A3 says the carry \"applies to the decline leads only\"; the Files-to-Change row says \"for the decline leads\"; REQ-001 enumerates only the three single-word refusals; the mechanism row points at `command-attach.ts:405`, which is now `:412`. T029 (`tasks.md:82`) implements the question carry, and the tests pin it at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:160-174,209-215`.\n- **Impact:** a reader planning or verifying from the spec is told an implemented, tested case is out of scope; the stale pointer also costs a lookup. No behaviour impact.\n- **Fix recommendation:** amend REQ-001, the Out-of-Scope line, the Files-to-Change description, A3 and the pointer; optionally restate AC-001/AC-006 to name the added forms.\n- **Disposition:** active advisory.\n- **Finding class:** doc-drift. **Scope proof:** the five spec lines are the only statements about the carry; T029 and the code/test lines above implement it. **Affected surface hints:** 027 spec, 027 acceptance criteria; no code.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **WS-1 (P1, before release):** close the two-word item gap in `COMMAND_OR_LIST`; pin it at the predicate and at a hub/CLI row; re-run the single-word refusal, question and request controls. The fix is small; the risk is over-widening the item and swallowing a request, so the request rows are the guard.\n2. **WS-2 (P2, advisory):** amend the 027 spec so the requirement, scope, file table and assumption describe the code as shipped; correct the moved pointer. Doc-only.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The or-list contract should state whether the list item is one token or a tracked command (which makes `/doctor:ci report` part of the grammar), so the next reader does not have to infer it from the constant.\n- The confirming-round additions (article on a listed item, `command` after it, question over a list) belong in the phase requirement, not only in appended task rows.\n- Keep the clause-separation rule explicit: a second use verb opens a new clause and keeps its command.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Test first: add `do not run /doctor:ci report or /doctor:ci scaffold` to the refusal table and to the `offers no hub command for %s` table; run the guards suite and the CLI probe and see the command offered before the change.\n- Widen the item once, re-run the guards suite, the typecheck and the mention probe; keep the request rows (`use A or B`, `use A, not B`, `do not run A, run B or C`, `do not run A or run B`) green.\n- Amend the 027 spec in one pass; run the packet's doc checks; re-run the confirming round on the amended range.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\n|----------|--------|----------|------------------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | REQ-001's three refusals and the request controls behave as written at the CLI; T028/T029 implement the article and question forms | SAC4C-P1-001 (multi-word item) and SAC4C-P2-001 (spec text lags the implemented question carry) |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | T028 and T029 are `[x]` with evidence that matches the diff, code and test rows; the nine added test rows match the two task contracts | AC-001 and AC-006 still read `Unmet`; expected until AC-011 closes this round |\n\n### Overlay protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `advisor-recommend.md:33` describes `attachCommand` accurately and makes no or-list claim; no skill doc contradicts the code |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | no agent surface in this lineage's scope |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | no runtime mirror in this lineage's scope |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | no playbook surface in this lineage's scope |\n\n**AC_COVERAGE:** exempt. The review target's root has no `acceptance-criteria.md` and no `implementation-summary.md`; the acceptance gates live in the phase children (027 is the one this round touches), so the advisory signal does not apply at this level.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The two-word item fix could be folded into phase 026's stored-number freeze if the lead prefers one edit window; it is not a blocker for this lineage's report.\n- The reducer's registry attributes SAC4C-P2-001 to `correctness` because the delta finding row carried no `dimension` field; the report and iterations attribute it to `traceability`. Counts and severity are unaffected; a reducer re-run with a dimension-bearing row would correct the label.\n- No resource-map gate: `resource-map.md` is absent at the target root, so the gate and its report section are skipped by contract.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0; failed pivots: 0; audited overrides: 0.\n- Swept directions: none. Saturated directions: none.\n- Selected review directions: correctness (iteration 1, or-list grammar), traceability (iteration 2, spec and docs), maintainability with security cross-reference (iteration 3).\n- Remaining frontier: none — all four configured dimensions covered.\n- This section records breadth only and does not alter the verdict or the registry.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*\n\n- Search methods used: direct reads of the changed files and callers, exact `grep` for `commandOnlyMentioned` call sites and doc claims, `git show`/`git diff` for the base-commit line numbers, a real-module probe under Node type stripping, and the advisor CLI on the round's prompts.\n- No corpus file was opened; no holdout prompt was read or printed.\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence summary\n\n| Iteration | Focus | newFindingsRatio | P0/P1/P2 | Verdict |\n|-----------|-------|------------------|----------|---------|\n| 1 | correctness | 1.00 | 0/1/0 | CONDITIONAL |\n| 2 | traceability | 1.00 | 0/0/1 | CONDITIONAL |\n| 3 | maintainability + security | 0.00 | 0/0/0 | CONDITIONAL |\n\n- The last ratio clears the 0.10 threshold, but iteration 3 is the cap, so the legal stop is `maxIterationsReached`; the convergence telemetry is preserved.\n- Active P0: 0. Active P1: 1. Active P2: 1. Resolved: 0.\n\n### Coverage summary\n\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4/4).\n- Files reviewed: `command-attach.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `fusion.ts` and `advisor-recommend.ts` as callers, the 027 spec/tasks/AC, and three skill docs as doc context.\n\n### Ruled-out claims\n\n- The fix over-suppresses requests (seven request shapes kept their command).\n- The article allowance breaks an existing question row (zero-iteration match when no `or`).\n- The shipped build lacks the fix (the dist copy carries it).\n- A missing hub-level row hides a distinct failure (the predicate is the only mention branch).\n- A changelog entry is missing (phase 025 owns release notes).\n- ReDoS or regex injection (bounded iteration, escaped name, constant leads).\n- Comment-hygiene violation or duplicated grammar (one constant, no ids).\n\n### Sources reviewed\n\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 48f03b5013 868b185e76 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (and the guards test; README as doc context).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:356-441,459-514`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:145-274`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1200-1246`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:500`.\n- `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:195-205,239,244-252,279,356,378-390`, `tasks.md:57-82`, `acceptance-criteria.md:56,61,66`.\n- `review/verify-4/report.md`, `review/review-brief-4c.txt`, `review/review-scope-4c.txt`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`.\n- Live probes: `tmp/probe-or-list.mjs`, the advisor CLI rows, and `git show` of the two prior commits.\n\n### Cross-reference appendix\n\n**Core Protocols:** `spec_code` partial; `checklist_evidence` partial (reasons above).\n**Overlay Protocols:** `feature_catalog_code` pass; `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `playbook_capability` notApplicable.\n\n### Release-readiness state\n\n`in-progress` — the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` (not `converged`) and one P1 remains active.\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report — scorer-attach closing round, pass four\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL**\\n- **hasAdvisories: false** (the verdict is CONDITIONAL, not PASS with advisories)\\n- **Active findings: 0 P0, 1 P1, 1 P2**\\n- **Review scope:** the `scorer-attach` rows of `review-scope-4c.txt` — `command-attach.ts` and `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` — plus the docs that describe them, for commit range `48f03b5013..868b185e76`. Inspection was read-only; all writes are inside `review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/`.\\n- **Iterations:** 3 of 3 (cap reached and recorded as `maxIterationsReached`; the last iteration's `newFindingsRatio` was 0.00, below the 0.10 threshold).\\n- **Operator review focus (verbatim):**\\n\\n> Closing round of review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and follow specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4c.txt: it names the scope file, the commit range, which files your lineage reviews and the checks. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\\n\\nThe round's own checks resolve as follows. **Refusals over an or-list** carry no command, with the article and the word `command`, and the plain form, at the predicate, `attachCommand` and the advisor CLI. **Questions over an or-list** carry no command; **requests over a list** keep their command. The exception is a list whose non-final item is a two-word `/doctor:` command, which is the active P1. The `offeredAs`, shell-read, heredoc, Codex-read and live-holdout checks belong to the sibling `accuracy-runner` lineage and to `verify-4`, and were not re-graded here; the docs this lineage read agree with the scorer code.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required: an active P1 remains.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAC4C-P1-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word /doctor command still publishes the refused command\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:380\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAC4C-P2-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The remediation spec still calls the question-over-an-or-list unreproduced and out of scope, and describes the carry as decline-only\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:239\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"traceability\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-1\\\",\\n      \\\"order\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"SAC4C-P1-001\\\"],\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Extend the or-list item grammar to a two-word command, or record the limit; pin both the predicate and the CLI row.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"WS-2\\\",\\n      \\\"order\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"findingIds\\\": [\\\"SAC4C-P2-001\\\"],\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Amend the remediation spec's requirement, scope, file table and assumption to match the implemented question carry, and correct the moved line pointer.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": \\\"Record that an or-list refusal or question covers every joined command the tracked table can express, and state whether two-word /doctor commands are in scope. Record the confirming-round additions (article form, question over a list) in the phase requirement rather than only in the appended tasks.\\\",\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add a test row for `do not run /doctor:ci report or /doctor:ci scaffold` to the or-list refusal table and to the `offers no hub command for %s` table; expect no command on either surface.\\\",\\n    \\\"Widen `COMMAND_OR_LIST`'s item to an optional second word, or derive the item from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, then re-run the single-word rows, the request rows and the CLI probe.\\\",\\n    \\\"Amend `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`: REQ-001, the Out-of-Scope line, the Files-to-Change description, A3 and the mechanism pointer (:405 to :412).\\\",\\n    \\\"Re-run the confirming round over the amended diff; keep the ratio at or below 0.10.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"incomplete-fix\\\", \\\"doc-drift\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"commandOnlyMentioned\\\",\\n    \\\"typedCommandForTop\\\",\\n    \\\"withholdMentionedCommands\\\",\\n    \\\"rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst\\\",\\n    \\\"COMMAND_OR_LIST\\\",\\n    \\\"advisor CLI rows\\\",\\n    \\\"027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### SAC4C-P1-001 — P1, correctness\\n\\n- **Title:** An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word `/doctor:` command still publishes the refused command.\\n- **File:line:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:380` (applied at `:427`, `:429`, `:432`, `:439`).\\n- **Evidence:** `COMMAND_OR_LIST` matches a listed item as one token. `TRACKED_COMMANDS` ships 22 two-word `/doctor:` rows (`:143-178`), and `withholdMentionedCommands` compares a command row on its base name (`fusion.ts:1209`), so the second occurrence is unled. The CLI printed `[[\\\"command-doctor-ci-report\\\",\\\"/doctor:ci report\\\",\\\"run\\\"],[\\\"command-doctor-ci-scaffold\\\",\\\"/doctor:ci scaffold\\\",\\\"ask\\\"]]` for `do not run /doctor:ci report or /doctor:ci scaffold`; `typedCommandForTop('sk-code', …)` returned `/doctor:ci scaffold`. Both were reproduced at synthesis on the final tree.\\n- **Impact:** a reader who explicitly refuses two `/doctor:` commands is shown both refused commands on the top two rows, and the typed-command path can attach the refused command. Same symptom class as the SAC4B-P1-001 this round fixed, narrowed to the two-word rows.\\n- **Fix recommendation:** let the list item carry an optional second word (`(?: [a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?`), or match the item against the tracked command vocabulary; add the predicate row and a hub/CLI row; keep the request, question and second-use-verb controls green.\\n- **Disposition:** active; not a regression introduced by the fix (the pre-fix constant had the same single-token shape), but the fix's own contract sentence claims \\\"every command the list joins\\\".\\n- **Finding class:** incomplete-fix. **Scope proof:** item pattern at `:380`, call sites at `:427-439`, two-word rows at `:143-178`, base-name comparison at `fusion.ts:1209`. **Affected surface hints:** `commandOnlyMentioned`, `typedCommandForTop`, `withholdMentionedCommands`, `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, `COMMAND_OR_LIST`, advisor CLI rows.\\n- **Claim adjudication:** HUNTER found a positional multi-word gap; SKEPTIC checked REQ-001, A3/P049 and the 020 accepted limits and found no recorded exclusion; REFEREE kept P1 because the module's stated contract and a real CLI row reproduce it. Confidence high. Downgrade to P2 only with a recorded single-token or out-of-contract declaration.\\n\\n### SAC4C-P2-001 — P2, traceability\\n\\n- **Title:** The remediation spec still calls the question-over-an-or-list unreproduced and out of scope, and describes the carry as decline-only.\\n- **File:line:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:239` (also `:201`, `:248`, `:279`, `:384`).\\n- **Evidence:** the Out-of-Scope line says a question over an or-list was never reproduced; A3 says the carry \\\"applies to the decline leads only\\\"; the Files-to-Change row says \\\"for the decline leads\\\"; REQ-001 enumerates only the three single-word refusals; the mechanism row points at `command-attach.ts:405`, which is now `:412`. T029 (`tasks.md:82`) implements the question carry, and the tests pin it at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:160-174,209-215`.\\n- **Impact:** a reader planning or verifying from the spec is told an implemented, tested case is out of scope; the stale pointer also costs a lookup. No behaviour impact.\\n- **Fix recommendation:** amend REQ-001, the Out-of-Scope line, the Files-to-Change description, A3 and the pointer; optionally restate AC-001/AC-006 to name the added forms.\\n- **Disposition:** active advisory.\\n- **Finding class:** doc-drift. **Scope proof:** the five spec lines are the only statements about the carry; T029 and the code/test lines above implement it. **Affected surface hints:** 027 spec, 027 acceptance criteria; no code.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **WS-1 (P1, before release):** close the two-word item gap in `COMMAND_OR_LIST`; pin it at the predicate and at a hub/CLI row; re-run the single-word refusal, question and request controls. The fix is small; the risk is over-widening the item and swallowing a request, so the request rows are the guard.\\n2. **WS-2 (P2, advisory):** amend the 027 spec so the requirement, scope, file table and assumption describe the code as shipped; correct the moved pointer. Doc-only.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The or-list contract should state whether the list item is one token or a tracked command (which makes `/doctor:ci report` part of the grammar), so the next reader does not have to infer it from the constant.\\n- The confirming-round additions (article on a listed item, `command` after it, question over a list) belong in the phase requirement, not only in appended task rows.\\n- Keep the clause-separation rule explicit: a second use verb opens a new clause and keeps its command.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Test first: add `do not run /doctor:ci report or /doctor:ci scaffold` to the refusal table and to the `offers no hub command for %s` table; run the guards suite and the CLI probe and see the command offered before the change.\\n- Widen the item once, re-run the guards suite, the typecheck and the mention probe; keep the request rows (`use A or B`, `use A, not B`, `do not run A, run B or C`, `do not run A or run B`) green.\\n- Amend the 027 spec in one pass; run the packet's doc checks; re-run the confirming round on the amended range.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Unresolved drift |\\n|----------|--------|----------|------------------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | REQ-001's three refusals and the request controls behave as written at the CLI; T028/T029 implement the article and question forms | SAC4C-P1-001 (multi-word item) and SAC4C-P2-001 (spec text lags the implemented question carry) |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | T028 and T029 are `[x]` with evidence that matches the diff, code and test rows; the nine added test rows match the two task contracts | AC-001 and AC-006 still read `Unmet`; expected until AC-011 closes this round |\\n\\n### Overlay protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `advisor-recommend.md:33` describes `attachCommand` accurately and makes no or-list claim; no skill doc contradicts the code |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | no agent surface in this lineage's scope |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | no runtime mirror in this lineage's scope |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | no playbook surface in this lineage's scope |\\n\\n**AC_COVERAGE:** exempt. The review target's root has no `acceptance-criteria.md` and no `implementation-summary.md`; the acceptance gates live in the phase children (027 is the one this round touches), so the advisory signal does not apply at this level.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The two-word item fix could be folded into phase 026's stored-number freeze if the lead prefers one edit window; it is not a blocker for this lineage's report.\\n- The reducer's registry attributes SAC4C-P2-001 to `correctness` because the delta finding row carried no `dimension` field; the report and iterations attribute it to `traceability`. Counts and severity are unaffected; a reducer re-run with a dimension-bearing row would correct the label.\\n- No resource-map gate: `resource-map.md` is absent at the target root, so the gate and its report section are skipped by contract.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0; failed pivots: 0; audited overrides: 0.\\n- Swept directions: none. Saturated directions: none.\\n- Selected review directions: correctness (iteration 1, or-list grammar), traceability (iteration 2, spec and docs), maintainability with security cross-reference (iteration 3).\\n- Remaining frontier: none — all four configured dimensions covered.\\n- This section records breadth only and does not alter the verdict or the registry.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*\\n\\n- Search methods used: direct reads of the changed files and callers, exact `grep` for `commandOnlyMentioned` call sites and doc claims, `git show`/`git diff` for the base-commit line numbers, a real-module probe under Node type stripping, and the advisor CLI on the round's prompts.\\n- No corpus file was opened; no holdout prompt was read or printed.\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence summary\\n\\n| Iteration | Focus | newFindingsRatio | P0/P1/P2 | Verdict |\\n|-----------|-------|------------------|----------|---------|\\n| 1 | correctness | 1.00 | 0/1/0 | CONDITIONAL |\\n| 2 | traceability | 1.00 | 0/0/1 | CONDITIONAL |\\n| 3 | maintainability + security | 0.00 | 0/0/0 | CONDITIONAL |\\n\\n- The last ratio clears the 0.10 threshold, but iteration 3 is the cap, so the legal stop is `maxIterationsReached`; the convergence telemetry is preserved.\\n- Active P0: 0. Active P1: 1. Active P2: 1. Resolved: 0.\\n\\n### Coverage summary\\n\\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4/4).\\n- Files reviewed: `command-attach.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `fusion.ts` and `advisor-recommend.ts` as callers, the 027 spec/tasks/AC, and three skill docs as doc context.\\n\\n### Ruled-out claims\\n\\n- The fix over-suppresses requests (seven request shapes kept their command).\\n- The article allowance breaks an existing question row (zero-iteration match when no `or`).\\n- The shipped build lacks the fix (the dist copy carries it).\\n- A missing hub-level row hides a distinct failure (the predicate is the only mention branch).\\n- A changelog entry is missing (phase 025 owns release notes).\\n- ReDoS or regex injection (bounded iteration, escaped name, constant leads).\\n- Comment-hygiene violation or duplicated grammar (one constant, no ids).\\n\\n### Sources reviewed\\n\\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 48f03b5013 868b185e76 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (and the guards test; README as doc context).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:356-441,459-514`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:145-274`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1200-1246`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:500`.\\n- `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:195-205,239,244-252,279,356,378-390`, `tasks.md:57-82`, `acceptance-criteria.md:56,61,66`.\\n- `review/verify-4/report.md`, `review/review-brief-4c.txt`, `review/review-scope-4c.txt`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`.\\n- Live probes: `tmp/probe-or-list.mjs`, the advisor CLI rows, and `git show` of the two prior commits.\\n\\n### Cross-reference appendix\\n\\n**Core Protocols:** `spec_code` partial; `checklist_evidence` partial (reasons above).\\n**Overlay Protocols:** `feature_catalog_code` pass; `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `playbook_capability` notApplicable.\\n\\n### Release-readiness state\\n\\n`in-progress` — the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` (not `converged`) and one P1 remains active.\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794683941144,"end":1794683979624}}}}
